    ("18.4217", "★★★★ synchronous fiber-switch consumption implemented fiber_switch_now semantics HLE 1B80/1BA0 set g_switch_pending/g_switch_target outer dispatcher consumes after block nx known saves caller context with pc=nxt real resume point loads target continues pump triggers 10x more often n%2000 instead of 20000; 30M result exit=0 zero BADMEM GXM=0 40s only 2 real switch events MSW sync switch -> 848367C0 pc=81198BE8 r0=848367C0 fiber lifecycle loop then MSW sync switch -> 84846860 pc=8127B950 main app loop then stays main loop PCRING 8127C0E8 812B2A80 8127C0F8 8127B950; DIAGNOSIS switch machinery now correct and stable but fiber we drive 848367C0 entry 0x81198BE8 is app lifecycle loop NOT boot/loader fiber that performed GXM init nested-mode GXM=12; nested path reached GXM because fiber_exec_to_completion ran fiber created earlier with entry 0x81198C0A frame/boot loop from init wrapper to completion; NEXT enumerate g_fiber_list each fiber object entry [fiber+0x84] saved context pc at pump time identify fiber with entry 0x81198C0A or other boot entry drive THAT fiber schedule from pumper so GXM init executes again under stable synchronous-switch machinery."),
    ("18.4216", "★★★★ fiber-scheduling A/B completed (a) default pure deferral mode crash-free through 100M blocks exit=0 zero BADMEM 41s but GXM=0 guest spins app main loop pc=0x8127B950 blk=0x8127C0F8 T682A 119k PUMPSW ppc=0x812B1BA0 (b) old nested fiber_exec mode P5D_FIBER_NESTED=1 still reaches GXM=12 but crashes BADMEM va=0 block=0x8120682A ring 812B2A50 812068D8 8120682A 81198BEA; two experiments PUMPCONT keep loader fiber running when it asks to switch back to idle main fiber valid but slower 30M 99s still GXM=0 now disabled and caller-context save/restore around nested fiber execution rc_save/rc_restore 18.4216 replacing wrong fiber_restore_thread which restored MAIN-thread regs into fiber caller nested mode still crashes corruption elsewhere; CONCLUSION remaining crash in nested mode is shared-RecState register corruption in 0x812067a0 scheduler epilogue r5 becomes 0 deferral avoids it but starves loader fiber that performs GXM init; NEXT implement old-runtime P0-a properly one fiber_switch_now saves caller at switch point loads target sets dispatcher-consumed next-pc no nested execution no thread-reg restore drive loader fiber from BOTH main and pump loops at sufficient rate so GXM init executes fast probe instrument r5 at FUN_812067a0 entry/epilogue and at 0x8120682A confirm where zeroed compare GXM=12 nested path."),
    ("18.4213", "★★★★ P0-a implemented single deferred fiber-switch path no nested fiber_exec and main-loop switch consumption first crash-free 30M run exit=0 zero BADMEM but game now spins; changes HLE sceFiberSwitch/sceFiberRun main-loop paths no longer call fiber_exec_to_completion old nested path behind P5D_FIBER_NESTED=1 two round-robin nested-exec hacks disabled main loop consumes deferred switch after each block MSW 18.4213 saves current fiber context loads/rebuilds target context sets pc; result 2M/10M/30M all exit=0 badmem=0 crash=0 30M in 19s previously every run hit BADMEM va=2/va=0 within 2M init counts all 1 asserts=0; BUT GXM calls dropped to 0 boot flow no longer reaches loader/GXM path and run spins pc=0x8127B950 blk=0x8127C0F8 fib=84846860 FRAMEDUMP 30M T682A scheduler-poll probe 119,753 hits pump passes 18,000 only 2 MSW switches consumed pump keeps stopping on switch requests PUMPSW switch_to=84846860 ppc=812B1BA0; crash fixed but sceFiberSwitch now returns immediately instead of suspending caller until switched back old runtime n_fiber_switch saves only at call site pc=svc+2 sets force_npc SVC wrapper does not return r0 in new context guest scheduler/loader fiber not driven correctly; NEXT implement old-runtime single fiber_switch_now(s,target) semantics save current fiber with pc=block next pc load target context set dispatcher-consumed next-pc override so caller of sceFiberSwitch does not resume immediately pump/main consume it restoring loader-fiber progress and GXM path expect GXM>0 again."),
    ("18.4212", "★★★★★ old-runtime semantics port #1 the r0=2 pump corruption is ELIMINATED; (a) sceKernelCheckCallback 0x812B2AC0 now NOOP by default old runtime binds n_noop its cooperative-yield behaviour was our invented semantics source of PUMPSW/cross-fiber context writes P5D_CB_YIELD=1 restores old yield for A/B; (b) pump-end save guard pump refuses to store live context into g_fctx[f2] when g_cur_fiber != f2 FSAVE-REJECT 18.4212 direct entry of f2_pc=0x81207344/r0=2 corruption; 2M-block result 12s PUMPSW=0 H7344-BAD=0 FSAVE-REJECT=0 init counts all 1 asserts=0 fiber corruption path gone; NEW DETERMINISTIC BLOCKER 2M 12s BADMEM guest va=0x00000000 block=0x8120682A FUN_812067a0+0x8A scheduler epilogue ring 812B1B70 812067B6 81206... plus CANARY-CLOBBER A0DFFFDC v=00000000 blk=811E5928 x998 stack canary slot zeroed in 0x811E5928 callback frame and T682A scheduler-loop flood 120,773 lines probe at 0x8120682A r0=0 r14=8120682A sp=A0DFFFD8; next target canary/stack-corruption + scheduler-poll loop not fiber switching; recorded full port plan old runtime P0-a remove nested fiber_exec_to_completion single fiber_switch_now+g_next_pc consumed by outer dispatcher P0-b fiber_save owner/sp/pc guards P1 LwMutex create returns 0 zeroes 0x20-byte work no hle_malloc lock/unlock return 0 no deref timeout no quantum preemption while locked P4 assert default abort-in-place whitelist; efficiency 2M run+diag cycle ~15s each validated in one fast iteration."),
    ("18.4211", "★★★★ efficiency infrastructure one-command symbolized diagnostics + deterministic checkpoint regression and key discovery 2M-block run 12s reproduces same blocker as 30M run 110s; bottlenecks (a) every 30M validation ~110s (b) each round hand-wrote one-off Python log parsers 5-10 min (c) non-determinism M669 fixed forced repeated runs; new tooling tools/diag.py one command parses harness stdout/stderr groups INITW/ASSERT/BADMEM/CRASH/PUMPSW/H7344/GXM/FRAMEDUMP symbolizes every address via func_index.tsv/function_bounds.json function+original source file takes last WD pcring thumb-disassembles first BADMEM block prints ~2s or --json for CI; tools/run_checkpoints.py runs harness fixed block counts clean env hacks off wall-clock off extracts structured snapshot exit code init counts asserts GXM framectr BADMEM va/block list pcring hash sha256 last line compares baseline C:/dev/tmp/_chk/baseline.json --update writes baseline stdout line tolerance because aborting process may lose buffered tail lines; validated run_checkpoints --only 2000000 = 11.6-12.0s repeated runs PASS identical pcring hash b7547b75ad50a6d0 identical badmem va=0x2 block=0x81207344 init counts all 1 asserts 0; 2M checkpoint already hits same M670 blocker debug iteration loop drops from ~110s + manual analysis ~10-15min to ~12s run + ~2s diag ~15s total ~20-40x faster 30M reserved for milestone validation; efficiency rules: use 2M checkpoint for blocker matching never write ad-hoc parsers use diag.py every fix must pass checkpoint regression batch probes per run prefer porting empirically-validated old runtime semantics over re-deriving"),
    ("18.4210", "★★★★★ r0=2 corruption source pinpointed a fiber switch that happens inside the pump pass and its bad context is saved as fiber2 f2_pc=0x81207344; instrumentation (a) pre-pump context snapshot FCtx f1_pre right after saving suspended fiber at pump start restore uses snapshot instead of possibly-clobbered g_fctx[f1] 18.4210 (b) diagnostics pre_pc/pre_lr/pre_r0/pre_sp restored pc loader callback [0x81513DEC] f2_pc (c) PUMPSW guard pump stops pass when g_fiber_switch_to/g_fiber_flag_return armed instead of silently dropping request; captured restore log n=1..12 normal pre_pc=81198BF2 pre_lr=81198BEE pre_r0=2 pre_sp=A0DFFFF0 restored_pc=81198BF2 cb=811E5929 f2_pc=8120766A n=13 pre_pc=81207612 pre_lr=81207648 pre_r0=A0D7FD90 f2_pc=81207344 n=14 pre_pc=81207344 pre_lr=81198BEE pre_r0=00000002 pre_sp=A0DFFFF0 f2_pc=81207612 after one pump pass fiber2 saved context already has pc=0x81207344 next pump start captures same pc as main fiber snapshot then bad block executes BADMEM va=2; PUMPSW stop pump pass switch_to=84846860 flag_return=0 ppc=8120766A proves fiber switch to f1 0x84846860 requested inside pump why pump writes wrong context into fiber table; verified [0x81513DEC] stays 0x811E5929 correct callback FUN_811E5928 whose bl 0x81207344 at 0x811E595E passes r0=0x816CDA30 valid pointer so r0=2 not from loader callback path; NEXT fix HLE fiber switch semantics inside pump defer to main/fiber_exec switch handling or proper full save/restore that does not overwrite g_fctx[f1] so f2_pc never becomes 0x81207344 r0=2"),
    ("18.4209", "★★★★ deterministic pump scheduling + first capture of r0=2 bad dispatch; (1) pump pass wall-clock budget >80ms made interleaving load-dependent same binary produced different blockers va=2 at 0x81207344 vs va=0 at 0x8120682A changed to block-count-only default g_pump_wallclock P5D_PUMP_WALLCLOCK=1 restores; two consecutive 30M runs bit-identical 34,635 stdout lines same blocker same pc ring; (2) first capture bad dispatch probe on post-pump re-dispatch path pc=s.r[15] probe fn=gbn(pc) H7344-BAD pc=81207344 r0=00000002 r1=812B4150 r2=0 r3=848367C0 lr=81198BEE sp=A0DFFBA0 fib=848367C0 loop=3 faulting block reached from restored fiber1 context pc=0x81207344 lr=0x81198BEE r0=2; (3) semantics faulting guest code 0x81207344 push {r4,lr} ldr r0,[r0] movs r1,#1 movs r2,#0 blx 0x812B2830 pop {r4,pc} where 0x812B2830=sceKernelLockLwMutex HLE harness case r0=0 lock-mutex wrapper expects mutex-object pointer r0=2 invalid; loader helper 0x811E5CDA push {r4,lr} ldr r0,[0x81513DEC] cbz blx r0 pop likely invocation path; static value callback global [0x81513DEC] in p5d_true.elf is 0x811E5929 not 0x81207344 either saved fiber context inconsistent restored pc/lr pair from mid-callback or global clobbered next verify; NEXT validate/repair pump saved fiber1 context guard restore if restored pc/lr implausible keep executing current fiber loop dump [0x81513DEC] during run check HLE Fiber/LwMutex handle semantics"),
    ("18.4208", "★★★★★ double-initialization root cause found and fixed fiber2 pump loop was force-resetting fiber2 context to user entry on first pump pass re-executing app-init second time; new g_loop_site dispatch-loop tag; INITW initEntry-A-336 #1 loop=0 then #2 loop=3 same init entry once in dispatch loop 0 fiber_exec once in loop 3 fiber2 pump both caller lr=0x81198C18 fiber 0x84846860; pump code f1=g_cur_fiber save f1 f2=other if(pump_first||c2.r[15]==0) force-reset c2 to entry 0x81198C0A even though fiber2 already executed context saved first pump discarded re-ran from entry replaying init triggered all five singleton already initialized asserts; FIX 18.4208 (note b) record last fiber whose context genuinely saved by execution g_f2_seen=g_cur_fiber in fiber save path only force-reset when fiber has NOT actually run f2_ran=(g_f2_seen==f2) if((pump_first&&!f2_ran)||c2.r[15]==0u) reset else resume saved ctx pump_first=0; RESULT 30M run clean baseline assert HLE fix PMP2 fiber2 RESUME saved ctx pc=8120766A f2_ran=1 pc=811E5EE8 pc=811E5ECE init sequence exactly once ALL FIVE ASSERTS DISAPPEAR run advances past to new later blocker BADMEM guest va=0x00000002 block=0x81207344 block 81207344 push {r4,lr} ldr r0,[r0] movs r1,#1 movs r2,#0 blx 0x812B2830 pop {r4,pc} called with invalid object pointer r0=2 guest VA 0x2 small handle/index used as pointer next root cause"),
    ("18.4207", "★★★★ public repository published https://github.com/kaimeng114514/P5D-PC user-created repo branch main; published content authoritative research/status record and our own engine source only README .gitignore docs/P5D_MASTER.md 32.8 MB all milestones corrections docs/P5D_DIGEST.md docs/P5D_OPERATION_CHECKLIST.md docs/P5R_ANDROID_REFERENCE.md docs/RELEASE_COMPLIANCE.md docs/_MD_INDEX.md curated tools release_audit.py kb_audit.py kb_lookup.py kb_ledger_audit.py verify_doc_integrity.ps1 run_kb_audit.ps1 run_all_regressions.ps1 AOT recompiler generators engine/recompiler/_gen_split.py _gen_batch2.py static-recompilation runtime/HLE source engine/runtime/recomp_harness.cpp old-runtime GXM->Vulkan backend + memory modules engine/gxm/* engine/mem/* engine/common/*; excluded by release-compliance policy M662 docs/RELEASE_COMPLIANCE.md all game files eboot.bin p5d_true.elf data.cpk vita.cpk GFDPSP2.GSC movies/audio all game-derived recompiled code batch_*.cpp *.o recomp_harness.exe all game-derived SPIR-V spv_all logs/dumps evidence bitmaps; repository verified with tools/release_audit.py must PASS before publishing"),
