    ("18.4185", "★★★★ FUN_811DEAB4 / 0x811DE912 fully decoded -1 from type-3 path because descriptor +0x18/+0x1c zero [struct+0x1c] end ptr <= [struct+0x18] current ptr r3 stays -1 return: [OBJ24] probes pc=811DEAB4 r0=3 r1=1 r2=A05FFDB8 lr=811C6C90 FUN_811DEAB4 type=3 flags=1 ptr=&stack-size malloc(0x24) memset 0 stores +0x10=type 0003 +0x12=flags 0001 if type>0 stores +0x18=*ptr ptr=A05FFDB8 fiber2 stack slot; then pc=811DEB34 r4=84FEC040 struct 00000000 x4 00010003 00000000 x5 i.e. +0x18=0 +0x1c=0 +0x20=0 and pc=811DEB44 r0=FFFFFFFF confirms 0x811DE912 returned -1; decoded 0x811DE912 len=[r6+0x10] type 3 checks r5=[r6+0x18] vs lr=[r6+0x1c] cmp r5,lr bhs keep r3=-1 r4=r3 return r4 both fields 0 returns -1 immediately; size argument from *ptr=[A05FFDB8] is 0 caller lr=0x811C6C90 0x811C6Cxx render/model callback passed zero size; NEXT trace caller 0x811C6C8x where size should come from likely CPK file read/size query returning 0 [CONSUME] FHRead calls=1 bytes=62100 far too little for full boot fix file-read/size path descriptor real size endian conversion completes"),
    ("18.4184", "★★★★ runaway endian conversion explained converter called with length r2=0xFFFFFFFF (-1) because length provider 0x811DE912 takes return -1 path struct field [r6+0x12] bit0 is 0: [XSWAP] probe block 0x811DD4BC r0=84FEC040 r1=84FEC040 r2=FFFFFFFF r3=FFFFFFFF r4=84FEC040 r5=A05FFDB8 lr=811DEB4E sp=A05FFDA0 fib=84846860 struct header hdr +0=0 +0x18=0 +0x1c=0; call site 0x811DEB3A r0=r4 r1=r4 r2=0x10 bl 0x811DE912 -> r2=r0 returned length -> 0x811DEB46 r0=r4 r1=r4 r2=length bl 0x811DD4BC converter; decode 0x811DE912 r6=r0 r4=r2 r7=r1 r0=ldrh [r6+0x12] r0&=1 if r0==0 r0=-1 return so bit0 of struct+0x12 zero returns -1 caller passes straight to converter loops count 0xFFFFFFFF walking r0 upward until leaves Region B at 0xA2000000 harness BADMEM; M643 unbounded length really -1 sentinel from uninitialized/invalid structure descriptor struct 0x84FEC040 +0x12 flag clear size fields zero asset descriptor not populated by loader before conversion; NEXT trace who allocates/fills struct 0x84FEC040 caller above 0x811DEB34 which load/decompress step sets [struct+0x12] bit0 likely file-read/decode HLE returns short leaves descriptor zero fix so length provider returns real length conversion completes matrix init frame loop"),
