    ("18.4178", "★★★★ wait object captured at loop body r4=0x84FEDA00 160-byte guest calloc buffer lr=0x811E6A2E state int16 at +4; diagnostic bypass reveals next blocker execution stops advancing at n~360000: [LOOP8CC] probes loop-body block 0x811830CC fiber_exec dispatch + main loop + [DWATCH] object state; RESULT [LOOP8CC] EX r4=84FEDA00 r0=0 sp=A05FFDA8 lr=81207612 fib=84846860 ring alternating 81198BF6/81198BEA/811E5CDA/812067A0/812B1B70 fiber1 lifecycle <-> 811830CC/811830D6/8120760C/812B2A50 fiber2 DelayThread(0x7530) wait <-> 8120682A/81206832 scheduler; object [CALLOC] n=160 sz=1 -> 84FEDA00 +4 state starts 0 nothing guest writes 3; diagnostic unblocking FORCE3 once did not help state reset loop re-entered ALWAYS3 capped probes did not help UNCOND3 both dispatch sites force state=3 every time block 0x811830CC reached -> UNCOND3=2 then RUN STOPPED ADVANCING FRAMEDUMP ends n~360000 last pc=812067E8 blk=812067DC pc=812B1B70 blk=812067A0 wall 59s; state wait no longer blocker control proceeds stalls in blocking HLE/fiber path last trace sceFiberGetSelf 0x812B1B70 called from fiber manager 0x812067A0; NEXT dump last HLE stubs/PC ring at stall instrument 0x812067xx fiber-manager loop and HLE call ring when no block progress for N blocks identify new blocking API continue unblocking frame loop"),
    ("18.4177", "★★★ two measurements (1) throttling cooperative yield to 1/256 speeds run 2.75x 40s vs 110s per 3M but reintroduces fiber-scheduler resume crash BADMEM 0x8120682A va=0 reverted (2) with [INJECT] disabled fiber2 still sits in state-poll loop but 0x811830C8 entry probe no longer fires loop entered through dispatch path not covered by four probes next probe must target loop body block 0x811830CC: yield counters g_yield_tick & 0xFF == 0 cut ping-pong switching cost 3M 40s instead of 110s but run dies [BADMEM] guest va=0x00000000 unmapped block=0x8120682A ring 81206832 81207664 812B2 known fiber-scheduler canary/resume path throttle not safe yet; added [W8FEX] + [DWATCH] at fiber_exec dispatch s->r[15] = fn(s) fixed C++ ordering error moving g_watch_addr/g_watch_val declarations before dispatch loops; current INJECT-disabled 8M exit=0 ZERO BADMEM flags=00000002 GXM=12 frames=0 but FRAMEDUMP pc cycling 811830CC/811830DE <-> 8120760C/81207612 with 812B2A50 sceKernelDelayThread wrapper r0=0x7530 fiber2 still state poll loop yet neither [W8C8] nor [W8FEX] fires loop entry block 0x811830C8 reached through path probes do not see gbn_back/indirect/different nested loop; NEXT probe + dynamic watch at block 0x811830CC loop body in ALL dispatch loops capture object register r4 writer separately fix yield-throttle crash regain 2.75x speed"),
