    ("18.4102", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6m7: CALLBACK SIGNATURE FULLY CLARIFIED (opcode,arg1,OBJECT) WITH OBJECT IN r2 AND LOOKUP CALLER PASSES (4,0,0) DOUBLE MISMATCH: disasm 0x8116F3C6 push {r4,lr}; 8116F3C8 adds r1,r0,#0 r1=arg0=OPCODE; 8116F3CA adds r0,r2,#0 r0=arg2=OBJECT; cmp r1,#1 ble return0; cmp r1,#2 ble return0; cmp r1,#3 bgt return0 only opcode 3 proceeds; bl 0x81016818 accessor OBJECT; ldr r0,[r0,#0xC]; bl 0x8116F45E; return 0 -> callback API cb(opcode,arg1,object) dereferences [object+0xC]; lookup caller 0x81016404 movs r0,#4; movs r1,#0; movs r2,#0; blx cb -> opcode=4 rejected AND object=0 would assert even opcode3 DOUBLE signature mismatch confirming [manager+0xC] function pointer NOT lookup callback caller expects; only materialization 0x8116F3C7 at 0x8116E674 passed r1 into creation helper 0x8101612C - creation helper likely STORES it on created object possibly +0xC which is why ends up [manager+0xC]; but that slot real meaning different for manager type lookup expects; NEXT finish disassembling 0x8101612C (saw up to 0x810161A2) find exactly which offset receives r1 callback; re-examine lookup caller expected vtable layout (0x810164F4 expects (?,id) style find)"),
