    ("18.4092", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6lx: 4-ENTRY LOOP RUNS ONLY ONCE - CRASHES ON FIRST ITERATION - TABLE LIVES ON STACK WITH EMPTY HANDLERS: probe loop head 0x8116E6A8 fired exactly once n=1 r8=00000000 r7=812B414C r6=A05FFF10 r5=813AFC0C sp=A05FFF10 [sp]=8116F49B [sp+8]=00000000; r6=sp points 4-entry local table stack; r7=[r6]=[sp]=0x8116F49B address table entry 0 EMPTY function bx lr; r5=0x813AFC0C global manager slot; r8=0 first iteration; loop runs inner 2-call dispatch 0x8116F3E8 invoking empty entry handler then lookup(manager,0x7C) returns 0 because heap manager +8 registry empty then crashes 0x8116E6D6 bl 0x81016818 sb=0; loop never reaches iteration 2 FIRST iteration fails stack table entries empty/no-ops nothing registers any object; NEXT find who constructs 4-entry STACK table (write [sp..sp+0xC] just before 0x8116E6A8 likely copying four 0x8116F4xx handler addresses) verify all four empty handlers determine what SHOULD have registered object id 0x7C (registry filler still missing)"),
    ("18.4091", "static recompilation stage 6lw: SEGMENT MATH CONFIRMED 0x81555E98 IS BSS AND BOTH CANDIDATE FUNCTIONS 0x8117BCB0/0x81171EF6 BELONG TO DIFFERENT OBJECT SYSTEMS NOT CRASHING MANAGER: script 81555E98 in segment v=81325000 filesz part no BSS part YES; disasm 0x8117BCB0 movw r0,#0x6AF0; movt r0,#0x8155; ldr r7,[r0,#4]; cmp r7,#0; beq 0x8117BD4C walks list rooted at global 0x81556AF0 +4 head SKIPS when [0x81556AF4]==0; 0x81171EF6 bl 0x81172EAE; movw r0,#0xFCA0; movt r0,#0x813A; ldr r4,[r0]; ldr r5,[r4,#8] processes object reached from global 0x813AFCA0; neither touches crashing heap manager 0x84896B6C nor +8 registry NOT registry filler; several independent global object/list systems (0x813AFC0C manager, 0x81555E98, 0x81556AF0, 0x813AFCA0); NEXT go back to crashing manager - instrument 4-entry loop at 0x8116E6A8 (print r8/r7/r6 and [manager+8] each iteration) and store at 0x8116E6DC (print sl) see exactly what loop tries read where object would have to come from"),
    ("18.4090", "static recompilation stage 6lv: 0x81555E98 LIES IN BSS (ZERO-INITIALIZED OUTSIDE FILE-BACKED DATA) FIELDS MUST BE FILLED AT RUNTIME YET NO WRITER FOUND: ELF PT_LOAD extents segment 1 vaddr 0x81000000 filesz 0x00321810 file-backed up to 0x81321810; segment 2 vaddr 0x81325000 filesz 0x0021BA74 file-backed up to 0x81540A74 memsz 0x003AA4A0 BSS extends 0x816CF4A0; 0x81555E98 > 0x81540A74 inside BSS ZERO at load time must be initialized by CODE runtime; earlier precise grep only READS of 0x81555E98 no store no memcpy; possibilities (a) initializing writes via DIFFERENT base register expression not grepped (pointer received from another global/function not literal 0x8155<<16|0x5E98) (b) 0x81555E98 part of larger struct whose base computed elsewhere (0x81555xxx global context initialized as block); NEXT (1) verify segment math script reports containing segment whether address in filesz or BSS (2) search generated blocks code writing near 0x8155xxxx large memset/memcpy (block-level wr32 base 0x8155xxxx) (3) disassemble 0x8117BCB0 and 0x81171EF6 (two calls following dead init sequence) candidate registry-fillers"),
    ("18.4089", "static recompilation stage 6lu: PRECISE SCAN - 0x81555E98 HAS ONLY 8 REFERENCES ALL READS ALL IN 0x81173xxx FAMILY AND IS DIFFERENT SYSTEM FROM MANAGER 0x84896B6C: grep exact low-half 0x5E98 found 8 sites all batch_011.cpp blk_8117304E reads [x+0xC], blk_8117306A reads [x+8] -> 0x8115D1D0, blk_81173088 reads [x+8], blk_811730AE reads [x+8], blk_811730E2 reads [x+0xC] plus two more reads; NO store to [0x81555E98+8] anywhere (grep wr32 near 0x5E98 with +8 = 0 hits) i.e. +8 only READ never written runtime - value can only come from ELF data-segment initial content; clarifies 0x81555E98 global and manager object 0x84896B6C heap created 0x8116E674 TWO DIFFERENT systems: lookup that crashes on heap manager whose +8 registry zero because hle_malloc zero-fills it and NOTHING registers objects into it; NEXT (a) dump ELF data-segment initial value at 0x81555E98+8 see whether valid pointer and what points to (b) disassemble 0x8117BCB0 and 0x81171EF6 (calls follow dead 0x81184776 in init sequence - one may be real registry filler reachable from another live call site)"),
    ("18.4088", "static recompilation stage 6lt: 0x81184776 IS DEAD CODE - NO DIRECT CALLER NO LITERAL REFERENCE NO MOVW/MOVT SITE: dedicated scan ZERO references to value 0x81184776 anywhere image - no .data/.rodata dword equals it no movw #0x4776 / movt #0x8118 pair materializes it; together with earlier grep (no return 0x81184776u call site) proves 0x81184776 and by extension its callee 0x8101949C in that path is DEAD function game never calls - matches probe result both counters 0; registration entry hypothesis WRONG real registry filler elsewhere; NEW DIRECTION find actual writers of registry container [0x81555E98] - stores to [0x81555E98+8] array struct pointer and array count field; also writers of +0xC/+0x10 fields seen earlier; trace writer of [0x81555E98+8] backwards: whichever code path stores valid array-struct there is real registration path and its absence/failure explains empty registry"),
    ("18.4087", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6ls: CONFIRMED BY PROBES - WHOLE REGISTRATION CHAIN NEVER RUNS IN 10M BOOT: added entry probes 0x81184776 and 0x8101949C reran 10M both counters ZERO (84776 count 0, 1949C count 0) BADMEM unchanged va=0x0000000C block=0x81016836; during entire 10M block run game NEVER executes init sequence 0x81184776 NEVER runs pre-registration init 0x8101949C therefore NEVER calls register+init 0x8117306A - registry array [0x81555E98+8] stays empty lookup(manager,0x7C) returns 0 0x81016818 hits assert path; fully explains crash registration sequence simply never invoked in our run; NEXT since 0x81184776 no direct caller search INDIRECT references to its address - scan movw/movt producing 0x81184776 (0x4776 low half) and .data/.rodata dword 0x81184776; if in init-callback table find who initializes and invokes that table (likely boot/init path never reach because earlier step skipped)"),
    ("18.4086", "static recompilation stage 6lr: HLE-STUB FIX 0x812B11B0 write non-zero / 0x812B11A0 return 0 DID NOT CHANGE CRASH - BADMEM STILL va=0x0000000C block=0x81016836: added two cases recomp_harness.cpp ~line 359 relinked harness-only reran 10M exit=3 same BADMEM guest va=0x0000000C unmapped block=0x81016836 ring_va=0000000C 812B28A0 8120735C 81173... 81016E6CA 810164F4; GXM=0 FIOS=0; CONCLUSION missing HLE stubs NOT blocker - most likely whole registration chain never runs at all: M544 established 0x81184776 init sequence calling 0x8117306A has NO direct caller so 0x8101949C and HLE calls may never be reached before crash; NEXT instrument entries of 0x81184776 and 0x8101949C entry counters rerun 10M CONFIRM whether execute at all; if not find how 0x81184776 supposed invoked (indirect function pointer table or call from code never reach) look for alternative place should fill registry [0x81555E98+8]"),
    ("18.4085", "★★ static recompilation stage 6lq: ROOT CAUSE OF MISSING REGISTRATION CONFIRMED - HLE STUBS 0x812B11B0/0x812B11A0 NOT IMPLEMENTED AND 0x812B11B0 MUST WRITE NON-ZERO OUTPUT: recomp_harness.cpp hle_call line 320 default r0=0 success unknown NIDs; case list implements malloc/free/memcpy/memset/strlen/strcpy LwMutex fibers GXM Fios AppUtil Ctrl Display but NO case 0x812B11B0 or 0x812B11A0 (grep none); both fall to default return 0 doing NOTHING; 0x8101949C blx 0x812B11B0; cmp r0,#0; bne fail; ldr r0,[sp,#0x40]; cbz r0,fail - after call READS stack output [sp+0x40] bails if zero; stub neither fills buffer nor returns meaningful so [sp+0x40] stays 0 -> bails 0x810194F6 registration skipped -> registry array [0x81555E98+8] empty -> lookup(manager,0x7C) returns 0 -> 0x81016818 assert -> BADMEM; FIX PLAN add two cases hle_call (1) 0x812B11B0 write non-zero dword to guest address s->r[0] output buffer return 0 (2) 0x812B11A0 return 0 success; relink harness-only ~1 min run 10M check 4-entry table loop gets past first lookup BADMEM should move again"),
    ("18.4084", "★ static recompilation stage 6lp: PRE-REGISTRATION FUNCTION 0x8101949C CALLS TWO HLE SYSTEM FUNCTIONS 0x812B11B0 AND 0x812B11A0 AND 0x81184776 HAS NO DIRECT CALLER: disasm 0x8101949C push {r4,r5,lr}; sub sp,#0xC4; canary; movw r0,#0xAA4; movt r0,#0x8154; str r1=0,[r0] clears global 0x81540AA4; movs r2,#0; movt r2,#0x357; movs r1,#0x80; blx 0x812B11B0 HLE CALL; cmp r0,#0; bne 0x810194F6 failure path; ldr r0,[sp,#0x40]; cbz r0,0x810194F6; add r0,sp,#0; blx 0x812B11A0 ANOTHER HLE CALL -> pre-registration init calls TWO system stubs 0x812B11B0 and 0x812B11A0; if either returns 0/failure bails to 0x810194F6 whole registration sequence skipped; ALSO 0x81184776 init sequence calling register function has NO direct caller - may be called indirectly function pointer or never called; NEXT check harness implements 0x812B11B0/0x812B11A0 (likely sceAppUtil/sceSysmem init) then instrument 0x8101949C entry/exit and 0x81540AA4 global whether succeeds in 10M run"),
    ("18.4083", "static recompilation stage 6lo: REGISTER+INIT 0x8117306A EXACTLY ONE CALLER BLOCK 0x8118477C INSIDE INITIALIZATION SEQUENCE FUNCTION 0x81184776 REGISTERS JUST ONE OBJECT NO LOOP: disasm caller neighborhood 8118476E bx lr; 81184770 push {r4,lr}; bl 0x8108955A; pop; 81184776 push {r4,lr}; 81184778 bl 0x8101949C; 8118477C bl 0x8117306A REGISTER+INIT; 81184780 bl 0x8117BCB0; 81184784 bl 0x81171EF6; 81184788 bl 0x810995A0; 8118478C movs r0,#0; pop {r4,pc} -> 0x81184776 linear boot/init sequence NO loop calls 0x8101949C first registers+initializes ONE object via 0x8117306A then three more init calls; either (a) 4 objects lookup expects registered inside 0x8101949C or later init calls or (b) sequence should run 4 times from loop in ITS caller; NEXT find who calls 0x81184776 (caller may be loop or app-init entry) disassemble 0x8101949C runs immediately BEFORE registration may create/prepare registry objects"),
    ("18.4082", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6ln: FOUND REGISTRATION FUNCTION ARRAY APPEND 0x8115D1D0 AND 0x8117306A IS REGISTER+INITIALIZE OBJECT: disasm 0x8115D1D0 push {r4,lr}; adds r4,r0,#0 container; ldr r1,[r4,#4] capacity; ldr r0,[r4,#8] count; adds r0,#1; bl 0x812B0E8E; ldr r1,[r4] array base; rsb r2,r0,r0,lsl #2 (r2=3*count); str r0,[r4,#8] store new count; add.w r0,r1,r2,lsl #2 (base+12*count); movs r1,#0; str r1,[r0,#8] zero-init new entry; pop {r4,pc} -> APPENDS 12-byte entry to array described by r4 ([+0]=base [+4]=capacity [+8]=count) THE REGISTRATION MECHANISM; 0x8117306A calls it with r0=[0x81555E98+8] global container array-struct pointer followed by 0x8116E734 manager state init, 0x81173602 more init reads global 0x813AFCDC, 0x81004B8E init another object reads global 0x81328B04 -> 0x8117306A REGISTER+INITIALIZE ONE OBJECT; registry lookup misses is array at [0x81555E98+8]; if array count stays 0 nothing registered; NEXT find callers/loop of 0x8117306A who registers 4 objects instrument [0x81555E98+8] count field see whether 0x8117306A ever runs"),
    ("18.4081", "static recompilation stage 6lm: SINGLE CALLER OF 0x8116E734 IS BLOCK 0x8117307A INSIDE FUNCTION 0x8117306A READING GLOBAL STRUCTURE 0x81555E98: caller block blk_8117307A s->r[14]=0x8117307Eu; return 0x8116E734u; neighborhood function 0x8117306A: push {r4,lr}; r0=0x81555E98; r0=[r0+8]; bl 0x8115D1D0; 0x8117307A bl 0x8116E734; 0x8117307E bl 0x81173602; 0x81173082 bl 0x81004B8E; 0x81173086 pop {r4,pc}; PRECEDING function 0x8117304E-0x81173066 manipulates SAME global r0=[0x81555E98+0xC]; bl 0x81015FD6; r0=[0x81555E98+0x10]; r5=0; [0x81555E98+0xC]=r5; bl 0x81018E48; [0x81555E98+0x10]=r5 -> 0x81555E98 global context/manager structure fields +0xC/+0x10 swapped/cleared +8 passed into manager-state init chain; NEXT disassemble 0x8115D1D0 consumes [0x81555E98+8], 0x81173602, 0x81004B8E called right after manager init; instrument read of 0x81555E98 see actual field values runtime - tell whether global context initialized correctly where 4 objects should be registered"),
    ("18.4080", "static recompilation stage 6ll: CORRECTION - 0x81016296 IS FIELD ACCESSOR READ [obj+4] NOT GET/CREATE HELPER; 0x8116E734 HAS EXACTLY ONE CALLER: disasm 0x81016296 push {r4,lr}; adds r4,r0,#0; bne 0x810162B4; bl 0x8115F832 assert line 0x11C; ldr r0,[r4,#4]; pop {r4,pc} - simply returns [obj+4] after null/flag assert; MANY call sites (8+ blocks) consistent with template accessor instance; therefore in 0x8116E734 r4=[manager[0]+4]; if 0 failure path 0x8116E86A; else r5=[r4+0xC] zero-inits/float-inits r5; state initializer reads nested field chain manager[0] -> +4 -> +0xC only proceeds when each non-NULL; 0x8116E734 EXACTLY ONE caller whole translated program block ending at batch_011.cpp:10758; NEXT identify caller block/address disassemble its neighborhood - single entry starts manager-state initialization surrounding code may be missing step creating/registering 4 objects BEFORE 4-entry table loop"),
    ("18.4079", "static recompilation stage 6lk: FOUND MANAGER STATE-INITIALIZATION FUNCTION 0x8116E734 AND NEW GET/CREATE HELPER 0x81016296: disasm 8116E734 push.w {r4,r5,r6,r7,r8,sb,sl,fp,lr}; sub sp,#0x1c; canary; movw r0,#0xFC0C; movt r0,#0x813A; ldr r4,[r0] GLOBAL MANAGER 0x813AFC0C; cbnz r4,0x8116E774; bl 0x8115F832 assert line 0x127; reload r4; 8116E774 ldr r0,[r4] manager[0]; 8116E776 bl 0x81016296 NEW GET/CREATE HELPER -> r4; 8116E77A adds r4,r0; beq 0x8116E86A FAILURE PATH if 0; adds r0,r4; bl 0x81016818 accessor -> r5=[r4+0xC]; zero-init/float-init r5 fields [r5+0x18]=0 [r5+0x1C]=0 [r5+0x20]=0 [r5+0x24]=0 [r5+0x6C..0x78]=floats manipulate [r5+0x10]/[r5+0x14] flags -> manager STATE INITIALIZER; calls 0x81016296 returns valid object or 0 failure; NEXT disassemble 0x81016296 see whether another find/create-by-id like 0x810164F4 what does on miss; find who calls 0x8116E734 (caller may be missing init step runs BEFORE 4-entry table loop)"),
    ("18.4078", "static recompilation stage 6lj: CORRECTION - M537 THIRD READER 0x812A582E FALSE POSITIVE; TABLE ONLY 2 READERS 0 WRITERS: direct disasm 0x812A5820 shows 812A582E movw r1,#0xfc10; 812A5832 adds r5,r0,#0; 812A5834 movt r1,#0x8131; 812A5838 bl 0x812AEA4C -> builds 0x8131FC10 NOT 0x813AFC10 (movt immediate 0x8131 different page); earlier robust scan matched pair patterns loosely flagged site but actual constant 0x8131FC10; CORRECTED FACTS 0x813AFC10 exactly TWO readers (0x8116F3EA dispatcher, 0x8116F432 entry allocator), ZERO writers, no memcpy - purely static data entries 0/1 intentionally empty bx lr stubs; registration lookup expects does NOT come from this table at all dynamic-fill hypothesis stays refuted; NEXT revisit assumption [manager+0xC]=0x8116F3C7 right callback - check whether manager object TYPE wrong (maybe DIFFERENT constructor should have run storing proper opcode-4 handler) or whether callback accepted range [1..3] by design and caller opcode 4 is type-tag rather than opcode"),
    ("18.4077", "static recompilation stage 6li: SCANNED FOR WRITERS OF 0x813AFC10 TABLE - NO WRITER FOUND BUT THIRD READER AT 0x812A582E: robust Thumb scan movw #0xFC10 / movt #0x813A pairs exactly THREE sites 0x8116F3EA (0x8116F3E8 dispatcher), 0x8116F432 (0x8116F3FE entry allocator), 0x812A582E NEW site 0x812Axxxx region outside 0x8116xxxx app module; literal scan word 0x813AFC10 NO references and no store/memcpy into table in translated code; CONCLUSION 0x813AFC10 dynamically filled hypothesis probably WRONG - table stays static image bytes (entries 0/1 intentionally empty bx lr stubs); registration lookup expects must come from DIFFERENT mechanism (another list/table) not 0x813AFC10 record handlers; NEXT disassemble around 0x812A582E third reader 0x812Axxxx region may be real registry/init path reads same table from different module understanding may reveal where 4 objects supposed to come from"),
    ("18.4076", "static recompilation stage 6lh: 0x8116F3FE IS ALLOCATE-ONE-ENTRY-BY-INDEX COPYING 24-BYTE RECORDS FROM 0x813AFC10 TABLE; TABLE HANDLERS MAY NEED DYNAMIC FILLING: disasm 8116F3FE push {r4,r5,r6,r7,lr}; sub sp,#0x14; adds r4,r2,#0 (r4=INDEX); adds r5,r1,#0; adds r6,r0,#0; movs r0,#0x20; bl 0x8115D79C ALLOC 0x20; bl 0x8115D36A error report; movw r2,#0xFC10; movt r2,#0x813A; rsb r1,r4,r4,lsl #2 (r1=3*index); adds r7,r0; str r4,[r7] entry[0]=index; add.w r1,r2,r1,lsl #3 (0x813AFC10+24*index); adds r0,r7,#4; movs r2,#0x18 copy 24 bytes -> each entry 0x20-byte object word[0]=index then 24 bytes copied from 0x813AFC10; loop 0x8116E6A4-0x8116E704 creates 4 such entries (r8=0..3); BEFORE lookup inner loop 0x8116E698-0x8116E6A2 calls 0x8116F3E8 = movw r1,#0xFC10; movt r1,#0x813A; rsb r0,r0,r0,lsl #2; ldr.w r0,[r1,r0,lsl #3]; blx r0 invoke 24-byte table record handler for index r0 twice; our table entries 0/1 EMPTY functions (bx lr, movs r0,#0; bx lr) so inner calls do nothing -> nothing registered -> lookup misses; NEW HYPOTHESIS 0x813AFC10 table DYNAMICALLY FILLED at runtime (register/init path never run) static base image merely contains empty defaults; NEXT find who WRITES 0x813AFC10 table (stores into 0x813AFC10+24*idx or memcpy from elsewhere) what should trigger it"),
    ("18.4075", "static recompilation stage 6lg: FOUND [sl+0xC] WRITE SITE AND MAPPED FULL LOOP STRUCTURE AROUND FAILING LOOKUP: after lookup 8116E6D0 bl 0x810164F4 (lookup(manager,0x7C)); 8116E6D4 mov sb,r0; 8116E6D6 bl 0x81016818 accessor obj=sb -> sl=[sb+0xC]; 8116E6DA mov sl,r0; 8116E6DC str.w r8,[sl]; 8116E6E2 str.w r4,[sl,#4]; 8116E6E8 str.w sb,[sl,#8]; 8116E6EE bl 0x8116F3FE; 8116E6F2 str.w r0,[sl,#0xc] WRITE +0xC = result 0x8116F3FE; 8116E6F6 bl 0x8116F480; 8116E6FA add.w r8,r8,#1; 8116E6FE adds r6,#4; 8116E700 cmp.w r8,#4; 8116E704 blo 0x8116E6A8 LOOP 4 times -> loop builds 4-entry table each iteration lookup(manager,0x7C) get object via 0x81016818 accessor fills [sl]=r8 [sl+4]=r4 [sl+8]=sb [sl+0xC]=0x8116F3FE(); CRITICAL crash at 0x8116E6D6 bl 0x81016818 with sb=0 BECAUSE lookup returned 0 - loop FIRST iteration cannot get object registry [manager+8] empty; loop expects 4 objects already exist/registered; NEXT disassemble 0x8116F3FE and 0x8116F3E8 (inner 2-iteration dispatch) and loop head 0x8116E6A8-0x8116E6CA - find what should create/register those 4 objects before this loop"),
    ("18.4074", "static recompilation stage 6lf: SECOND CALLBACK HYPOTHESIS REFUTED - 0x8116FA67 NOT OPCODE-4 HANDLER: disasm 0x8116FA66 push {r4,lr}; 8116FA68 ldr r0,[r0,#0x34]; 8116FA6A bl 0x8116F75E; 8116FA6E pop {r4,pc} - simply reads field [obj+0x34] tail-calls 0x8116F75E NO opcode comparison; so not opcode-4-capable callback; whole find-another-callback direction probably WRONG; RETHINK 0x8116F3C6 checks (cmp r1,#1 ble; cmp r1,#2 ble; cmp r1,#3 bgt) may not be opcode test but TYPE/STATE test; and [manager+0xC]=0x8116F3C7 written during creation but game may LATER OVERWRITE this slot with real per-type handler (our run never reaches/executes); NEXT find every store into [manager+0xC] (or [obj+0xC] where obj registry manager) - search generated blocks for writes to +0xC on pointer loaded from global manager slot 0x813AFC0C; if such overwrite exists never runs in 10M = missing init step"),
    ("18.4073", "static recompilation stage 6le: FOUND SECOND CALLBACK CANDIDATE (0x8116FA67) AND LEARNED 0x8101612C IS GENERIC HELPER: scan for movw/movt #0x8116 pairs in 0x8116F000-0x8116FFFF found exactly TWO callback materializations @8116E674 -> 0x8116F3C7 (traced) and @8116FA08 -> 0x8116FA67 (SECOND unseen callback); also 0x8101612C has MANY callers most pass r0=4 (or 0) with r1=0 (blk_810004A4 r0=0 r1=0; blk_81004B4A r0=4 r1=0; blk_81008222 r0=4 r1=0x81008371; blk_810206BA r0=4 r1=0) so 0x8101612C is GENERIC invoke callback(r1) with opcode 4 on object r0 helper and manager pointer only one kind of r0; r0=4 callers pass small TYPE/ID not heap pointer which explains add.w r6,r5,#0x14 makes r6=0x18 fake slot callback interprets as type id; NEXT disassemble SECOND callback 0x8116FA67 (Thumb entry 0x8116FA66) check whether IT handles opcode 4 - if so manager creation at 0x8116E674 should have used it instead of 0x8116F3C7 find where correct value should come from"),
    ("18.4072", "static recompilation stage 6ld: 0x8101612C FULL SEMANTICS = INVOKE CALLBACK WITH OPCODE 4 AND PROCESS RESULT; REFUSAL -> ERROR REPORT: disasm 8101612C push.w {r4,r5,r6,r7,r8,lr}; sub sp,#0x20; canary; 81016140 adds r4,r1,#0 (callback); mov r5,r0 (manager); add.w r6,r5,#0x14 (manager+0x14); bne 0x8101614E; movs r0,#0; strd r6,r0,[sp,#0x10] slot={manager+0x14,0}; add r3,sp,#0x10; movs r0,#4; movs r1,#0; movs r2,#0; blx r4 callback(opcode=4,r3=&slot); cmp r0,#0; beq 0x8101616E; ldr r7,[sp,#0x14] result callback wrote slot; cbnz r7; movs.w r7,#-1; cmp.w r7,#-1; bne 0x8101617A; movs r0,#0 return 0 failure; b 0x810161E4; cbnz r7,0x810161C0; bl 0x8115D614; adds r0,r6,#0; bl 0x8115D79C; bl 0x8115D36A ERROR REPORT -> function calls callback OPCODE=4 expects store result into slot {manager+0x14,0}; refusal drives r7=0 and ERROR REPORT then returns 0; our callback 0x8116F3C6 only handles opcode 3 refuses 4 -> error report -> return 0 -> subsequent lookup fails; CONCLUSION call site genuinely expects opcode-4-capable callback in r1 but caller 0x8116E674 hard-codes r1=0x8116F3C7; NEXT examine callback opcode-3 path 0x8116F45E understand slot {manager+0x14,0}; search ANOTHER manager class/constructor passing different callback (other movw r1 near manager creations) or verify [manager+0xC] not callback at all (callback comes from ARGUMENT r1 not [manager+0xC])"),
    ("18.4071", "static recompilation stage 6lc: HYPOTHESIS REFUTED - 0x813AFC10 TABLE IS NOT OPCODE HANDLER TABLE: TABLE4 @0x8116F4A6 = movs r0,#1; bx lr (returns constant 1), TABLE0 @0x8116F49A = bx lr empty, TABLE8 @0x8116F4E8 = push {r4,lr}; adds r4,r0,#0; bl 0x8115D614; adds r1,r4,#0; bl 0x8115D43C; pop = generic method-invoke wrapper like 0x8116F45E; so 0x813AFC10 VTABLE-like array of small methods NOT opcode 0..9 dispatcher and index 4 not opcode-4 handler; earlier guess WRONG; opcode-4-vs-callback-3 mismatch unexplained; NEXT read REST of 0x8101612C (only saw up to 0x8101615E; function longer) receives callback in r1 likely STORES it into manager object (maybe [manager+0xC] or another slot); also read rest of manager-creation caller after 0x8116E6D0 see whether DIFFERENT callback/table should be stored; decide whether correct callback value elsewhere (different vtable table in .data) should be written into [manager+0xC]"),
    ("18.4070", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6lb: OPCODE 4 USED IN AT LEAST TWO PLACES so callback [manager+0xC] handling only opcode 3 is WRONG FUNCTION: corrected understanding 0x8101612C NOT malloc 0x8C but another CALLBACK-DRIVEN operation disasm 8101612C push.w {r4,r5,r6,r7,r8,lr}; sub sp,#0x20; canary; adds r4,r1,#0 (callback arg r1=0x8116F3C7); mov r5,r0 manager; add.w r6,r5,#0x14; bne 0x8101614E; movs r0,#0; strd r6,r0,[sp,#0x10]; add r3,sp,#0x10; movs r0,#4; movs r1,#0; movs r2,#0; blx r4 CALL callback opcode=4 r3=&{manager+0x14,0}; cmp r0,#0; and 0x81016378 NOT init but field ACCESSOR push {r4,lr}; adds r4,r0,#0; bne; assert line 0x82; ldr r0,[r4,#0x10]; pop (reads [obj+0x10]); SO opcode=4 is normal opcode used by both 0x81016404 lookup and 0x8101612C create/op but callback 0x8116F3C7 only handles 3 rejects 4; CONCLUSION [manager+0xC] WRONG function pointer: correct callback should handle opcode 4; region opcode 0..9 jump table 0x813AFC10 index 4 = 0x8116F4A7 very likely real opcode-4 handler; NEXT disassemble 0x8116F4A7 (and other entries) confirm handles opcode 4; determine which vtable/table should have been stored into [manager+0xC] and why our run got 0x8116F3C7 (different object type created or wrong field written by init path)"),
    ("18.4069", "static recompilation stage 6la: FOUND MANAGER CREATION SEQUENCE AND IMMEDIATE LOOKUP THAT FAILS - disasm 0x8116E650-0x8116E6D0 movw r5,#0xFC0C movt r5,#0x813A (global slot 0x813AFC0C); ldr r0,[r5] existing manager?; cbz r0,0x8116E674; else assert line 0xEB; movw r1,#0xF3C7 movt r1,#0x8116 (callback 0x8116F3C7); movs r0,#0x8C object size; bl 0x8101612C CREATE; adds r6,r0; bl 0x81016378 INIT; str r6,[r0]; movs r1,#1; str r0,[r5] publish global manager; then ldr.w sb,[r5] sb=manager; cmp.w sb,#0 bne 0x8116E6CA else assert; ldr.w r0,[sb] (r0=[manager] self-reference); movs r1,#0x7C; bl 0x810164F4 = lookup(manager,0x7C) MISSES; manager created size 0x8C callback 0x8116F3C7 published to [0x813AFC0C] then IMMEDIATELY lookup id 0x7C misses because [manager+8] registry head still 0; NEXT disassemble create/init 0x8101612C and 0x81016378 supposed to lay out 0x8C-byte manager including callback at +0xC and registry at +8; find why +8 stays 0 (init call/HLE stub returns 0 or registration step elsewhere skipped)"),
    ("18.4068", "static recompilation stage 6l9: mapped dispatch family around failing callback - 0x8116F45E (opcode-3 handler target) generic object-method invoker push {r4,lr}; 8116F460 adds r4,r0,#0; 8116F462 ldr r0,[r4,#0x1c]; 8116F464 ldr r1,[r4,#0xc]; 8116F466 blx r1; 8116F468 bl 0x8115D614; 8116F46C adds r1,r4,#0; 8116F46E bl 0x8115D43C; 8116F472 pop {r4,pc} -> call [obj+0xC] with [obj+0x1C] as arg; region contains JUMP TABLE at 0x813AFC10 with 10 entries 0x8116F49B/49D/4A1/4A3/4A7/4AB/4AD/4AF/4E9/4F9 = complete opcode 0..9 dispatcher (ldr.w r0,[0x813AFC10+idx*8]; blx r0 style); callback [manager+0xC]=0x8116F3C7 SUBSET dispatcher only opcode 3 while fuller opcode table elsewhere; since 0x81016404 passes opcode 4 either [manager+0xC] WRONG function pointer for this manager object or object different type than caller expects; NEXT find who WRITES [manager+0xC]=0x8116F3C7 (store or vtable-like constant table) reveals manager object intended type/vtable; compare with what 0x810164F4 expects (find-by-id callback accepting opcode 4)"),
    ("18.4067", "static recompilation stage 6l8: MANAGER CALLBACK IS OPCODE DISPATCHER HANDLING ONLY OPCODE 3 but 0x81016404 passes opcode 4 so returns 0 immediately: disasm callback 0x8116F3C6 (value at [manager+0xC]): push {r4,lr}; 8116F3C8 adds r1,r0,#0; 8116F3CA adds r0,r2,#0; 8116F3CC cmp r1,#1; ble 0x8116F3E2; 8116F3D0 cmp r1,#2; ble 0x8116F3E2; 8116F3D4 cmp r1,#3; bgt 0x8116F3E2; 8116F3D8 bl 0x81016818; 8116F3DC ldr r0,[r0,#0xc]; 8116F3DE bl 0x8116F45E; 8116F3E2 movs r0,#0; pop {r4,pc} -> r1<=1 return 0; r1<=2 return 0; r1>3 return 0; only continues when r1==3; caller 0x81016404 passes r0=4 (81016434 movs r0,#4) and callback moves r0 into r1 so r1=4 -> bgt -> return 0 immediately; TWO POSSIBILITIES (a) [manager+0xC] NOT lookup routine for THIS operation (wrong vtable slot/wrong manager object type) (b) opcode convention in AOT run differs; NEXT disassemble 0x8116F45E (opcode-3 handler) learn convention, check OTHER dispatchers (region 0x8116F3E8+ contains jump table ldr.w r0,[r1,r0,lsl #3]; blx r0 at 0x8116F3E8 = switch table for another dispatcher); find correct lookup path for opcode 4 / correct manager object"),
    ("18.4066", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6l7: DECISIVE MANAGER AND CALLBACK VALID [manager+8] NULL LIST HEAD so OBJECT NEVER REGISTERED: [164F4] probe mgr=84896B6C id=0000007C [mgr+8]=00000000 [mgr+0xC]=8116F3C7 sp=A05FFF10 (n=1) single call; manager 0x84896B6C valid heap object, id 0x7C, [manager+0xC]=0x8116F3C7 valid CODE pointer lookup callback, but [manager+8]=0 NULL; lookup DID run callback got not found because manager table/list head at +8 EMPTY; object id 0x7C never REGISTERED into manager = missing registration/insertion step (init or add-object routine whose path never execute, or HLE-side object creation should insert into manager list); NEXT (a) disassemble callback 0x8116F3C7 confirm how walks [manager+8]; (b) find INSERT routine (block doing str obj,[manager+8] or similar) see whether it ever runs in 10M; if not find what should trigger it (init HLE call or missing object-creation path); fix so object id 0x7C registered before lookup"),
    ("18.4065", "static recompilation stage 6l6: LOOKUP HELPER 0x81016404 DELEGATES TO MANAGER CALLBACK - miss either manager==NULL or [manager+0xC]==NULL: disasm 81016404 push.w {r4,r5,r6,r7,r8,lr}; sub sp,#0x20; canary; 81016418 adds r6,r1,#0 (ID); 8101641A movs r5,#0 result; 8101641C adds.w r4,r6,#0x10; 81016420 cmp r0,#0; 81016424 beq 0x8101644A return 0 if manager==0; 81016426 ldr r3,[r0,#0xc] MANAGER CALLBACK; 81016428 cbnz r3,0x8101642C; 8101642A b 0x8101644A return 0 if callback==0; 8101642C mov lr,r3; 8101642E strd r4,r5,[sp,#0x10]; 81016432 add r3,sp,#0x10; 81016434 movs r0,#4; movs r1,#0; movs r2,#0; 8101643A blx lr invoke manager callback (r0=4,r1=0,r2=0,r3=&{id+0x10,0}) -> find object by id = manager-vtable style call [manager+0xC] is find function; if manager or callback 0 returns 0 (our miss); NEXT instrument 0x810164F4 entry (manager,id) print manager + [manager+8] + [manager+0xC] determine whether MANAGER itself NULL (trace where should have been created/initialized) or callback returns 0 (inspect callback target)"),
    ("18.4064", "static recompilation stage 6l5: 0x810164F4 IS FIND-OBJECT-BY-ID FUNCTION RETURNING 0 ON LOOKUP MISS: disasm 810164F4 push {r4,r5,r6,lr}; 810164F6 adds r5,r0,#0 (r5=manager/container); 810164F8 mov r4,r1 (r4=ID case 0x7C); 810164FA bne 0x81016514 else assert 0x8115F832 line 0x123; 81016514 ldr r6,[r5,#8]; 81016516 adds r0,r5; 81016518 adds r1,r4; 8101651A bl 0x81016404 LOOKUP; 8101651E adds r4,r0; 81016520 bne 0x81016526 found; 81016522 movs r0,#0; 81016524 b 0x81016540 RETURN 0 NOT FOUND; 81016526 bl 0x810168A6; 81016530 ldr r6,[r5,#0xc]; 81016534 movs r0,#2; blx r6 callback; 8101653E adds r0,r4 return found object -> NULL reaching accessor is simply MISS lookup(manager,0x7C) returned 0; NEXT disassemble lookup helper 0x81016404 see HOW it searches (linked list/table/hash) why id 0x7C not found - likely object never REGISTERED because init/register HLE path skipped or table/global uninitialized; fix registration/init so lookup succeeds"),
    ("18.4063", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6l4: TRACED NULL ONE LEVEL UP - RETURN VALUE OF 0x810164F4: [G18] entry probe fired exactly once r0=00000000 lr=8116E6DA prev=8116E6D4 sp=A05FFF10 cur=846867F0 -> NULL-passing caller block 0x8116E6D4; generated s->r[9]=s->r[0]; s->r[14]=0x8116E6DAu; return 0x81016818u -> accessor argument r0 is RETURN VALUE of PREVIOUS call (blk_8116E6CA s->r[0]=rd32(s,s->r[9]); s->r[1]=0x7C; return 0x810164F4u) -> 0x810164F4 returned 0/NULL; disasm region 8116E6A8 ldr.w sb,[r5]; 8116E6AC cmp.w sb,#0; 8116E6B2 bne 0x8116E6CA; ... bl 0x8115F832 (assert line 0x60); 8116E6CA ldr.w r0,[sb]; 8116E6CE movs r1,#0x7C; 8116E6D0 bl 0x810164F4 -> called with (r0=[sb], r1=0x7C) returns 0 reaching 0x81016818 accessor as obj=NULL -> assert -> crash; NEXT disassemble 0x810164F4 see why returns 0 (likely create/get-object failing possibly HLE stub returning 0 or list/table lookup miss); fix cause so returns valid object"),
    ("18.4062", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6l3: NEW BADMEM IS ANOTHER ASSERT PATH - 0x81016818 IS A FIELD ACCESSOR CALLED WITH obj=0: body 81016818 push {r4,lr}; 8101681A adds r4,r0,#0; 8101681C bne 0x81016836; 8101681E ... bl 0x8115F832 (error report strings 0x812EE708/0x812EE74C line 0x1AD); 81016836 ldr r0,[r4,#0xc]; 81016838 pop {r4,pc} -> r4=argument object pointer, adds r4,r0 sets flags, bne 0x81016836 NORMAL path (return [obj+0xC]) when obj!=0, when obj==0 reports error via 0x8115F832 (assert-style) then FALLS THROUGH to ldr [0+0xC] deliberate crash; game called accessor with obj=NULL hit own assert path; same pattern as earlier 0x8115F9D4 assert - prerequisite object never initialized; many callers 8+ blocks (0x81000502, 0x81000590, 0x810005B4, 0x81000696 ...) fastest localization instrument 0x81016818 entry (r0+LR+prev_blk) read fatal line find caller passing NULL; NEXT add probe run 10M identify caller check why object/field NULL (missing HLE init or earlier write)"),
    ("18.4061", "static recompilation stage 6l2: mapped function boundaries around new fault - disasm 0x810167A0-0x8101680A shows COMPLETE function there (canary check 810167FE cmp r0,r1; 81016800 bne 0x81016806; 81016806 blx 0x812B2810 __stack_chk_fail) then small leaf functions 0x8101680C ldr r0,[r0], 0x81016810 ldr r0,[r0,#8], 0x81016814 ldr r0,[r0,#4]; faulting block 0x81016836 lies in SEPARATE function whose prologue starts 0x81016818: 81016818 push {r4,lr}; 8101681A adds r4,r0 -> r4 = function argument r0; crash ldr r0,[r4,#0xc] with r4=0 means THAT function called with r0=0 (or prologue did not set r4 before tail ran); NEXT disassemble 0x81016818-0x81016838 completely see function body (what it does with r0 before tail) then determine who calls it with r0=0 - likely another uninitialized HLE object passed down (like earlier appAllocatorHandler chain) or generator edge case in this region"),
    ("18.4060", "static recompilation stage 6l1: analyzed new BADMEM after shift fix - guest va=0x0000000C unmapped block=0x81016836 ring 812B28A0 8120735C 81173... 81016E6CA 810164F4; generated blk_81016836 s->r[0]=rd32(s,s->r[4]+0x0C); s->r[4]=rd32(s,s->r[13]); s->r[13]+=4; { _pc=rd32(s,s->r[13]); s->r[13]+=4; return _pc; } -> fault ldr r0,[r4,#0xc] with r4=0 va=0xC; disasm confirms 0x81016836 is FUNCTION TAIL ldr r0,[r4,#0xc]; pop {r4,pc}; r4 never set by prologue in this path - either function entered from middle again (like earlier 0x811AC934) or prologue mov r4,r0 ran with r0=0; NOTE now in region 0x81016xxx new app module and old appMemoryHandler misaligned-pointer chain completely gone (shift fix worked); NEXT find prologue of this function (disassemble ~0x810167C0-0x81016838) see where r4 set (push + mov r4,r0 expected) determine whether entry-from-middle happening again or argument r0 legitimately 0/invalid"),
    ("18.4059", "★★★★ static recompilation stage 6l0: SHIFTED-OPERAND GENERATOR FIX WORKS - appMemoryHandler misaligned-pointer crash chain GONE and fault moved forward again: applied _shreg patch to _gen_batch2.py (helper + 7 branches add/sub reg+reg and 2-operand, and/orr/eor/bic reg+reg and 2-operand, cmn, cmp, tst), regenerated 26 batches (26/26 ok 432.7s) relinked ran 10M; RESULT old BADMEM va=0x001F8469 block=0x81207344 GONE; new BADMEM guest va=0x0000000C unmapped block=0x81016836 ring_va=0000000C: 812B28A0 8120735C 81173... 81016E6CA 810164F4 - fault moved to NEW region 0x81016xxx now small offset 0x0C instead of 0x1F8469; ring shows sceKernelUnlockLwMutex 812B28A0 -> 8120735C -> 81173... -> 0x81016xxx so past job-pool lock area into new app code; GXM=0 FIOS=0 still; NEXT analyze block 0x81016836 (va=0xC) disassemble block and 0x81016xxx region; 0xC suggests small struct offset/field computation (possibly another generator edge case with shifted/offset operands or genuinely uninitialized HLE object); fix and continue"),
    ("18.4058", "static recompilation stage 6kz: FOUND EXACT ALU BRANCH DROPPING THE SHIFT - _gen_batch2.py lines 643-667: add/sub/rsb branch elif m in (adds,add,addw,subs,sub,subw,rsbs,rsb) sub-cases (a) isi(1) and len(ops)==2 imm (b) isr(1) and isi(2) reg+imm (c) isr(1) and isr(2) -> _b = R(reg(2)) NO SHIFT HANDLING = our bug (d) immediates (e) 2-operand high-register form; and/orr/eor/bic branch follows line 696+; correct pattern to copy mem() lines 89-107 reads o.shift/o.mem.shift emits << / >> / arithmetic >>; FIX add helper _shreg(i) next to R()/reg() handling LSL/LSR/ASR/ROR via ops[i].shift (tuple or attrs type/value); use _shreg(2) instead of R(reg(2)) in (c) branch and _shreg(1) in 2-operand branch and similarly and/orr/eor/bic branch; NEXT apply patch regenerate all batches 7-10 min relink run 10M re-check appMemoryHandler BADMEM should be gone"),
    ("18.4057", "static recompilation stage 6ky: located exact generator code to fix shifted-ADD bug - emit() in _gen_batch2.py line 74 loaded into _gen_split.py by executing source up to main marker src[:main_idx] lines 16-20; inside emit mem(i) helper lines 89-107 DOES handle shifted memory operands reading o.mem.shift emitting + (idx << sv) / >> / arithmetic >> - MEMORY-operand shifts correct; bug only in ALU path: register-operand shifts (add.w Rd,Rn,Rm,lsl #4 i.e. ops[2] with .shift attribute) emitted as plain s->r[n]+s->r[m] with no shift; NEXT read ALU section of emit (add/sub/and/orr/eor/rsb/adc/sbc after line 200) add shifted_reg(i) helper mirroring mem() shift logic (LSL-><<, LSR->>>, ASR->arith >>, ROR->rotate) applied to Rm operand; regenerate 7-10 min relink rerun 10M - appMemoryHandler misaligned-pointer crash chain should clear"),
    ("18.4056", "★★★★ static recompilation stage 6kx: FOUND REAL ROOT CAUSE - GENERATOR BUG shifted-register ADD translated with shift lost (+2 instead of *17): probes [D3A6] r8=846968A4 [r8+4]=846968C0 r9=0 (n=1) r9=1 (n=2); [D3B2] r0_out=846968C0 r1=0 sb=0 (n=1) r0_out=846968C2 r1=2 sb=1 (n=2); [r8+4] stable 0x846968C0 difference purely from r9(sb)=0 vs 1 multiplied by 2 -> r0 = base + sb*2; BUT actual instruction 0x8115D3AA add.w r1,sb,sb,lsl #4 = sb+(sb<<4) = sb*17 NOT sb*2; generated blk_8115D3A6 s->r[1]=s->r[9]+s->r[9] - lsl #4 SHIFT OPERAND LOST; AOT generator drops shift on register-shifted ADD (likely other shifted-register ALU ops) producing sb*2 instead of sb*17 -> array index wrong -> container pointer 2 bytes off (much more wrong for larger sb) -> [obj+4] read misaligned -> 0x1F8469 garbage -> BADMEM; CORE GENERATOR BUG like earlier id_reg LR bug not game/object issue; FIX in _gen_split.py when emitting shifted-register ALU instructions (add.w Rd,Rn,Rm,lsl #N etc) apply shift to Rm operand s->r[d]=s->r[n]+(s->r[m]<<N) (analogously lsr/asr/ror and sub/and/orr/eor); regenerate all batches 7-10 min relink run 10M - appMemoryHandler crash chain should clear"),
    ("18.4055", "static recompilation stage 6kw: FOUND ARITHMETIC BUILDING CONTAINER POINTER r0=[r8+4]+(sb*17)*4 (ARRAY-INDEX WALK): blocks blk_8115D3A6 = s->r[0]=rd32(s,s->r[8]+4); s->r[1]=s->r[9]+s->r[9]; s->r[0]=s->r[0]+s->r[1] (generated uses r9+r9 for add), blk_8115D3B2 sets r1 from r7 ubfx+bfi, blk_8115D3BC stores r1 at [sp+4] sets r1=sl(r10) r2=fp(r11) r3=r5 calls 0x8115D8E0 (r0 NOT set in 0x8115D3BC flows from preceding blocks); disasm 8115D3A6 ldr.w r0,[r8,#4]; 8115D3AA add.w r1,sb,sb,lsl #4 (=sb*17); 8115D3AE add.w r0,r0,r1,lsl #2 (= [r8+4]+sb*68) = indexed array element inside structure at r8; observed difference only 2 (0x846968C0 -> 0x846968C2) does NOT match stride 68 -> either [r8+4] itself changed between calls or generated r9+r9 add wrong for real operand relationship; NEXT instrument blk_8115D3A6 print r8 [r8+4] r9/r1 resulting r0 on both invocations see which term changed; if [r8+4] changed find writer; if r9+r9 add mismatches guest operand fix generator/logic"),
    ("18.4054", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6kv: ONE MORE LEVEL UP - CALLER IS BLOCK 0x8115D3BC and SAME CALLER computed both 0x846968C0 (correct) and 0x846968C2 (+2) on different invocations: [D8E0] probe twice n=1 r0=846968C0 lr=8115D3C8 prev=8115D3BC r1=00200000 sp=A05FFF20 cur=846867F0 and n=2 r0=846968C2 lr=8115D3C8 prev=8115D3BC r1=00000028 sp=A05FFEF0 cur=846867F0; same caller block 0x8115D3BC (LR 0x8115D3C8) so caller r0 computation depends on STORAGE changed between two calls (global field/struct member/list node) - 0x846968C0 first then 0x846968C2 second; suggests shared data structure pointer field advanced/+2 by some code between calls (e.g. iterator over packed array of 2-byte elements or Thumb-bit adjustment stored back to memory); NEXT read block 0x8115D3BC generated code (and few blocks before) see exact instruction computing r0 - if load from [global+off] instrument/monitor that address find writer that adds 2 between calls; fix writer or read"),
    ("18.4053", "static recompilation stage 6ku: CLARIFIED CALLER LEVEL - 0x8115D8E0 IS A FUNCTION ENTRY and passes its own parameter r0 UNCHANGED (r7=r0 then r0=r7 bl 0x8115F7C2) so +2 NOT introduced here: disasm 8115D8E0 push.w {r4,r5,r6,r7,r8,sb,sl,lr}; 8115D8E4 ldr r6,[sp,#0x20]; 8115D8E6 adds r7,r0,#0; 8115D8EA adds r5,r3,#0; 8115D8EC mov r8,r2; 8115D8EE mov sb,r1; 8115D8F0 adds r0,r7,#0; 8115D8F2 bl 0x8115F7C2; container object 0x846968C2 misaligned pointer is ARGUMENT some caller passed INTO function 0x8115D8E0; 0x8115D8E0 may have multiple callers so efficient move instrument its entry print r0 + LR + prev_blk - one probe identifies caller supplying 0x846968C2; NEXT add probe run 10M read fatal line inspect caller pointer computation (+2 origin)"),
    ("18.4052", "static recompilation stage 6kt: located direct callers of lock-acquire helper 0x8115F7C2 - both in 0x8115D8xx region (matching BADMEM ring 8115D entries): block ending return 0x8115F7C2u at 0x8115D8F6 (batch_010:13388) and at 0x8115D934 (batch_010:13393); first caller tail s->r[8]=s->r[2]; s->r[9]=s->r[1]; r0=r7; s->r[14]=0x8115D8F6; return 0x8115F7C2u -> r0=r7 no +2 in tail; second caller tail also does not set r0 explicitly (saves r8/r9 returns); so +2 introduced in block(s) BEFORE these call sites that compute r7 and r0 i.e. inside 0x8115D8xx/0x8115D9xx; NEXT disassemble 0x8115D8C0-0x8115D940 inspect generated blocks how r7/r0 computed - look for adds rX,#2, ldrh/halfword loads, or Thumb-bit masked address, fix that specific computation"),
    ("18.4051", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6ks: DECISIVE - CONTAINER POINTER OFF BY +2 (MISALIGNED) which is why [obj+4] contains garbage: [7C2] entry probe fired twice n=1 obj=846968C0 [obj+4]=846968E0 sp=A05FFF00 cur=846867F0 and n=2 obj=846968C2 [obj+4]=001F8469 sp=A05FFED0 cur=846867F0; container pointer changed from ALIGNED 0x846968C0 (whose +4 field is valid lock object 0x846968E0) to MISALIGNED 0x846968C2 (=0x846968C0+2); reading [0x846968C2+4]=[0x846968C6] yields garbage 0x1F8469; clean pointer off-by-2/misalignment bug: somewhere container pointer computed as (correct pointer + 2) very likely Thumb-bit or half-word offset handling error or struct field read at wrong offset; NEXT find caller(s) of lock-acquire helper 0x8115F7C2 (grep return 0x8115F7C2u) inspect how they compute obj argument - look for +2/#2/halfword add or Thumb address adjustment on this pointer; fix computation and 10M should proceed past appMemoryHandler"),
    ("18.4050", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6kr: BAD POINTER IS STRUCT FIELD [obj+4] CORRUPTED BETWEEN TWO CALLS - blk_8115F7C8 = s->r[14]=0x8115F7CCu; return 0x811731D8u (r0 from preceding block); disasm function 0x8115F7C2 push {r4,lr}; 8115F7C4 ldr r0,[r0,#4]; 8115F7C6 cbz r0,0x8115F7CC; 8115F7C8 bl 0x811731D8 lock; 8115F7CC pop {r4,pc} -> LOCK-ACQUIRE helper argument r0 container object loads field [obj+4] actual lock object pointer and if non-zero passes to shared lock wrapper; crash value 0x1F8469 = CONTENT of [obj+4]; SAME caller had [obj+4]=0x846968E0 valid on first invocation and 0x1F8469 on second -> CONTAINER OBJECT or its +4 field CORRUPTED/REWRITTEN between two calls; NEXT instrument function entry 0x8115F7C2 print incoming obj pointer and [obj+4] at both invocations (whether obj lies on stack ~0xA05FFxxx/0xA0DFFxxx or heap ~0x84xxxxxx) determines stack-overlap/clobber vs heap-object corruption, find writer"),
