    ("18.4048", "static recompilation stage 6kp: 0x811731D8 IS A SHARED LOCK WRAPPER WITH 10+ CALLERS so need entry LR to discriminate: disasm 811731D8 push {r4,lr}; 811731DA bl 0x811732EE pure wrapper forwards r0 to LwMutex chain; callers many each computes r0 differently - blk_810160BA r0=r8, blk_810160F6 r0=r5, blk_8115C85C r0=r6+0x24, blk_8115C918 r0=[sp+0x10]+0x24, block before 0x8115CC34 r0=r9 (r9 built from 0x8155 globals), blk_8115CCC6 r0=0x81555414 global address; also found nearby 0x811731C0 refcount-release helper (ldr r1,[r4,#4]; subs r0,r1,#1; str r0,[r4,#4]; bne; adds r0,r4,#0; bl 0x811732E6); with 10+ callers fastest path instrument wrapper entry 0x811731D8 print r0 + LR + prev_blk - LR immediately identifies which caller passed 0x1F8469 then only that single caller needs analysis; NEXT add probe run 10M read fatal line inspect identified caller r0 computation (candidates field loads / +0x24 offsets / 0x8155xxxx global addresses - field+0x24 load most likely culprit)"),
    ("18.4047", "static recompilation stage 6ko: call chain continues upward - 0x811732EE has exactly ONE caller blk_811731D8 which also does NOT set r0: generated blk_811731D8 { g_cur_block=0x811731D8; push {r4,lr}; s->r[14]=0x811731DEu; return 0x811732EEu; /* bl */ }; r0 flows in from caller of 0x811731D8 as well; disassembly of thunk region confirms lock/semaphore wrappers over HLE: 0x811732A4 push {r4,lr}; ldr r0,[r0]; blx 0x812B2A60; pop (deref+HLE), 0x811732AE push {lr}; sub sp,#0xc; movs r1,#0; ldr r0,[r0]; movs r2,#2; str r1,[sp]; movs r1,#1; movs r3,#0; blx 0x812B2880 (event-flag wait), 0x811732C6 push {r4,lr}; ldr r0,[r0]; movs r1,#1; blx 0x812B2AE0 (sema signal); r0 passed down through several wrapper layers unchanged (0x1F8469) and each layer derefs [r0] -> bad value entered at TOP of wrapper family; NEXT grep return 0x811731D8u find caller(s) continue up until find block that COMPUTES r0 (field load/add/return value) = where 0x1F8469 built and fix belongs"),
    ("18.4046", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6kn: CAUGHT THE FATAL CALL SITE - [LW] cap 400 fatal invocation [LW] r0=001F8469 prev=811732EE lr=811732F4 r1=00000028 r2=00000004 sp=A05FFEB8 cur=846867F0 (n=107); REAL caller of LwMutex lock wrapper is block 0x811732EE (blk_811732EE = push {r4,lr}; s->r[14]=0x811732F4u; return 0x81207344u pure call thunk that does NOT set r0) -> r0=0x1F8469 ALREADY set before entering 0x811732EE; context r1=0x28 lock parameter/count r2=4 sp=0xA05FFEB8 cur=fiber2 0x846867F0 -> happens inside fiber2 job-pool worker path; preceding [LW] n=105 r0=0x816CDA30 prev=811E5928 n=106 r0=0x846968E0 prev=811732EE show same thunk used with VALID r0 -> thunk fine bad value comes from caller of 0x811732EE; NEXT find blocks that call 0x811732EE (grep return 0x811732EEu) inspect how they build r0 (likely struct field/list-node pointer) = origin of bogus 0x1F8469"),
    ("18.4045", "static recompilation stage 6km: LwMutex-wrapper entry probe shows FIRST 24 calls all use VALID pointers - crash call is later: [LW] fired 24 times r0=816CDA38 prev=811D9E84 lr=811D9E88 r2=0x10/0x20 cur=0 sp=82EFFE20 (n=1..4) and r0=84675654 prev=811F0AE4 lr=811F0B0A r1=1 r2=0 cur=0 sp=82EFFE30 (n=5..24); NOTE 0x816CDA38 = 0x816CDA30+8 exactly the request-queue mutex recorded in milestone M247 (r4=0x816CDA30) so lock path is real app code and wrapper works for normal objects; because [LW] probe capped at 24 the fatal call with r0=0x001F8469 did NOT appear (BADMEM unchanged) - happens on LATER invocation; NEXT raise [LW] cap to ~400 rerun 10M; fatal line will reveal prev_blk (real caller) and allow tracing its r0 source = pure data-collection step"),
    ("18.4044", "static recompilation stage 6kl: CORRECTION - blk_811AC9CC ALSO NEVER DISPATCHED; crash caller is a different sceKernelLockLwMutex call site: instrumented block 0x811AC9CC (print r8 + prev_blk + LR) ZERO output across 10M blocks; neither function entry 0x811AC934 nor block 0x811AC9CC executes - earlier inference that 0x811AC9CC calls LwMutex wrapper WRONG; actual BADMEM ring 8115F8AC 8115F8B8 8115D... -> 0x81207344 (LwMutex lock wrapper) so reached from DIFFERENT call site among 8 blocks return 0x81207344u (blk_811732EE, blk_811ABFE2, blk_811AC060 and others before 0x811AC48A); fatal r0=0x1F8469 produced by one of those; NEXT instrument LwMutex wrapper entry block 0x81207344 itself print r0, prev_blk (g_cur_block), LR - single probe directly identifies real caller and exact pc passed invalid pointer; then trace THAT caller r0 source (no more guessing)"),
    ("18.4043", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6kk: DECISIVE - function entry block 0x811AC934 NEVER DISPATCHED so execution enters function from MIDDLE and r8 is RESIDUAL GARBAGE: instrumented entry block 0x811AC934 print r0+LR reran 10M -> [AC934] ZERO output while crash block 0x811AC9CC (inside same function) DOES run and hits ldr r0,[r8] via LwMutex wrapper; guest never executes function prologue (mov r8,r0 and canary setup) yet executes blocks deep inside same function -> r8=0x1F8465 NOT a real argument RESIDUAL value from before entry i.e. execution flow entered middle of function (wrong indirect jump target or fiber/context restore resumed at pc inside function without prologue); reframes crash: likely AOT indirect-jump/return-address problem (blx LR fixed in generator but indirect JUMPS/blx-to-mid-function may still land incorrectly) or fiber restore problem NOT bad-pointer arithmetic; NEXT instrument block 0x811AC9CC and 0x811AC9C8/0x811AC9C4 print r8 and PREVIOUS block (g_cur_block) at entry determine how execution reached middle of 0x811AC934 (which block/pc jumped there) then fix that dispatch"),
    ("18.4042", "static recompilation stage 6kj: traced r8 one level up - it is function r0 argument and function called INDIRECTLY: disasm entry 811AC934 push.w {r4,r5,r6,r7,r8,sb,sl,lr}; vpush {s16,s17}; sub sp,#0x28; movw sl,#0x414C; movt sl,#0x812B; ldr r2,[sl]; str r2,[sp,#0x20] canary; adds r5,r1,#0; 811AC956 mov r8,r0 -> r8 = FIRST ARGUMENT r0 of function 0x811AC934; later blk_811AC9CC s->r[0]=s->r[8] calls LwMutex lock -> invalid pointer 0x1F8465 is exactly r0 passed INTO 0x811AC934; searches: return 0x811AC934u normal bl callers 0 hits, literal DWORD 0x811AC934 0 hits, literal 0x81513BD8 0 hits (global loaded via movw/movt not literal word); CONCLUSION 0x811AC934 reached INDIRECTLY blx via function pointer so must log entry LR; NEXT instrument block 0x811AC934 print r0 and s->r[14] return address - LR identifies caller and its class then follow that caller r0 source; caller may be job-pool worker dispatch via table or event callback"),
    ("18.4041", "★★ ported 4GM/4GN pool model into AOT harness (first step) but did NOT fix crash, which localizes the real source: implemented init_job_pools() per docs 4GM.1/4GM.3 called after gxmvk_init(): initializes pool table [0x8169E080]={0xA0039000,0xA005A000,0xA0115000}; pool2 +0x00=0x14 jobSema +0x04=0x15 cap +0x08=0x16 evt +0x0C=0xA0007000 LwMutexWork +0x10=1 state +0x14=0xA005B000 ring +0x18=0x2800 cap +0x1C/0x20=0 +0x24=0xA005A100 workers +0x28=4 +0x2C=0; pool3 +0x00=0x17 +0x04=0x18 +0x08=0x19 +0x18=8 +0x28=1; pool1 minimal; LwMutexWork@0xA0007000 attr/lockCount/holder=0; RESULT [POOL-INIT] printed but BADMEM UNCHANGED guest va=0x001F8469 unmapped block=0x81207344 ring 8115F8AC 8115F8B8 8115D... (2x); CONCLUSION r8 in blk_811AC9CC is NOT pool+0xC and does NOT come from pool table - pool init necessary infrastructure but not source; NEXT instrument block 0x811AC9CC and function prologue see where r8 loaded (note 0x811AC9A6-0x811AC9B6 loads global 0x81513BD8 stores [r6+4]; check whether r8 tracks that global or another field), log [0x81513BD8] and r8 value at 0x811AC9CC"),
    ("18.4040", "★★★★ USER-DRIVEN FULL HISTORY REVIEW - CONFIRMED WORK WAS DONE BEFORE BUT NOT PORTED INTO AOT HARNESS: prior design corpus doc line 9460 2D thread&job-pool model; line 34052 4GM job-pool pool 14-field complete map + job records/secondary queue/LwMutex/fiber structures + three-pool parameters; line 34109 4GN synchronous dispatch two paths + worker main loop 21 disassembly lines => can be copied; line 105912 5ZH solidified thread/job-pool model pool 9 fields + 32B records + two dispatch paths + wake semantics; lines 134174-134289 pool fields three pools measured 0xA0039000/0xA005A000/0xA0115000 worker loop LwMutexWork layout attr@0 lockCount@4 holder@8; milestone M247 request-queue producer FUN_811E5D82 r4=0x816CDA30 mutex lock 0x81207344 malloc 0x811DA534; CRITICAL GAP current AOT harness almost NONE ported: case 0x812B2910 r0=hle_malloc(64) CreateLwMutex, case 0x812B2830 r0=0 Lock, case 0x812B28A0 r0=0 Unlock one-liners; pool table 0x8169E080 NEVER initialized; Sema/EventFlag/Thread HLE absent; old eboot_probe.cpp not in C:/dev; CONCLUSION current crash invalid mutex pointer 0x1F8465 from r8 in blk_811AC9CC is SYMPTOM of missing subsystem (guest running real job-pool/worker path but AOT harness has no pool table/real LwMutex/sema/event-flag state -> garbage pointers); CORRECT DIRECTION port documented 4GM/4GN/5ZH model into AOT harness: (1) initialize pool table [0x8169E080] and three pools (2) implement real LwMutex attr/lockCount/holder guest-held per doc 3.3 (3) implement Sema/EventFlag/thread HLE with wake semantics (4) implement worker main loop dispatch per doc 4GN; NEXT read doc 4GM line 34052 and 4GN line 34109 and 5ZH line 105912 as spec then port step by step"),
