    ("18.4038", "static recompilation stage 6kf: identified function building invalid LwMutex pointer - crash block inside function 0x811AC46A: disasm 811AC46A push.w {r4,r5,r6,r7,r8,sb,sl,fp,lr}; sub sp,#0x54; movw r2,#0x414C movt r2,#0x812B ldr r2,[r2]; str r2,[sp,#0x50] save canary; 811AC47C mov fp,r0; 811AC47E add.w r5,fp,#4; 811AC482 adds r6,r1,#0; 811AC484 adds r0,r5,#0; 811AC486 bl 0x81207344 -> 0x811AC46A is LwMutex lock wrapper whose ARGUMENT r0 is LwMutex object pointer (r5=r0+4 then LockLwMutex(r0+4)); crash fp=0x1F8465 means CALLER of 0x811AC46A passed invalid mutex-object pointer; generated blk_811AC46A s->r[11]=s->r[0]; s->r[5]=r11+4; s->r[0]=r5; return 0x81207344u; NEXT find callers of 0x811AC46A (grep return 0x811AC46Au) trace where r0 mutex object pointer comes from - likely global object/struct field HLE never initialized or previous create call returning bogus handle; fix/initialize it"),
    ("18.4037", "static recompilation stage 6ke: found callers of 0x81207344 (LwMutex lock wrapper) - grep return 0x81207344u -> blk_811732EE, blk_811ABFE2, blk_811AC060 and block ending at 0x811AC48A; likely crashing site tail s->r[11]=s->r[0]; s->r[5]=s->r[11]+4; s->r[6]=s->r[1]; s->r[0]=s->r[5]; s->r[14]=0x811AC48Au; return 0x81207344u -> passes r0 = incoming r0 + 4 to LwMutex wrapper; crash r0 0x001F8469 = 0x001F8465 + 4 -> incoming r0 to block was 0x001F8465 also invalid -> invalid pointer built one or more levels above; NEXT disassemble/read full block containing 0x811AC48A and blocks reaching it find where r0=0x1F8465 came from - likely return value of previous bl (create/alloc/init returning bogus handle because HLE stub returns 0/partial) or struct field misread; fix source; 0x1F8465 may be resource/ID/size not address"),
    ("18.4036", "static recompilation stage 6kd: analyzed new BADMEM - block 0x81207344 = LwMutex lock wrapper disasm 81207344 push {r4,lr}; 81207346 ldr r0,[r0]; 81207348 movs r1,#1; 8120734A movs r2,#0; 8120734C blx 0x812B2830; 81207350 pop {r4,pc}; 0x812B2830 is sceKernelLockLwMutex; generated blk_81207344 s->r[0]=rd32(s,s->r[0]+0); s->r[1]=1; s->r[2]=0; s->r[14]=0x81207350u; return 0x812B2830u; fault at ldr r0,[r0] - caller passed r0=0x001F8469 NOT valid pointer; value dereferenced -> BADMEM va=0x1F8469; 0x1F8469 looks like structure member/small integer (offset or size) mistaken for pointer -> bug one level up in CALLER that built r0; ring 8115F8AC -> 8115F8B8 -> 8115D0A8 path through appMemoryHandler/mutex region; NEXT find block(s) that bl 0x81207344 (search generated batches for return 0x81207344u) inspect how r0 loaded there; likely cause structure field read from wrong base (e.g. [rX+0x60C] like blk_8115F8AC reads) or uninitialized HLE mutex/object pointer; fix source"),
    ("18.4035", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6kc: ABORTSKIP FIX WORKS - GUEST MOVED PAST appAllocatorHandler INTO appMemoryHandler: moved r0 override to REAL block entry pc==0x8115F9D0, reran 10M; deliberate-null-write BADMEM va=0 block=0x8115F9D4 GONE; new BADMEM guest va=0x001F8469 unmapped block=0x81207344 ring 8115F8AC 8115F8B8 8115D... another big step forward (different module, 0x81207344 = main-loop pump block); ALSO output contains NEW REAL GAME STRING E:/P3DP5D/xrd757/program/app/app_system/system/appAllocatorHandler/appMemoryHandler.c:%d (plus earlier appAllocatorHandler.c and ASSERT:%s x3) - confirming guest now executing appMemoryHandler code path (memory manager init/validation); GXM=0 FIOS=0 still; NEXT analyze new BADMEM at block 0x81207344 with va=0x001F8469 - va looks like small pointer (0x1F8469) probably structure member or size field misread as address; disassemble block and ring (0x8115F8AC/0x8115F8B8/0x8115D...) fix value source"),
    ("18.4034", "static recompilation stage 6kb: first [ABORTSKIP] attempt on WRONG pc - forced r0=0 at pc==0x8115F9D2 but BADMEM still hits block 0x8115F9D4 because 0x8115F9D2 is NOT a block entry: block starts at 0x8115F9D0 (cmp r0,#0; beq 0x8115F9D8 same block as conditional branch, fallthrough block 0x8115F9D4) so override ran at pc never dispatched; ALSO output contains string ASSERT:%s - confirming guest executing own ASSERT/fatal-error reporting machinery (appAllocatorHandler.c message passed to it); NEXT move r0 override to pc==0x8115F9D0 (real block entry) or on block reaching 0x8115F9D0 from 0x8115F9CA (i.e. at 0x8115F9CA/0x8115F9D0) then rerun 10M; deliberate null-write should be skipped and guest should continue past appAllocatorHandler"),
    ("18.4033", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6ka: NEW BADMEM 0x8115F9D4 IS A DELIBERATE NULL-WRITE/ASSERT-PATH: disasm 8115F9CA push {r4,lr}; 8115F9CC bl 0x8115F7E0; 8115F9D0 cmp r0,#0; 8115F9D2 beq 0x8115F9D8; 8115F9D4 movs r0,#0; 8115F9D6 str r0,[r0]; 8115F9D8 pop {r4,pc}; generated blk_8115F9D4 s->r[0]=0x0u setf_nz wr32(s,s->r[0]+0u,s->r[0]) = writes 0 to address 0 ON PURPOSE; classic assert/fatal-error idiom: call checker 0x8115F7E0 and if returns NON-ZERO deliberately null-deref; guest NOT randomly crashing - DETECTED ERROR CONDITION from 0x8115F7E0 taking own deliberate abort path; fix upstream: find what 0x8115F7E0 returns and why reports failure (init/validation routine whose prerequisite HLE call returned unexpected value e.g. size/allocator/thread state check); NEXT disassemble 0x8115F7E0 and callees find value/condition returns non-zero fix HLE/prerequisite so returns 0 success and guest continues"),
    ("18.4032", "★★★★ INDIRECT-CALL LR FIX WORKS - MALLOC NOW SUCCEEDS AND FAULT MOVED AGAIN: patched generator (_gen_split.py for idreg emit s->r[14]=<last.address+last.size> before return id_reg), regenerated 26 batches (26/26 ok 433s) relinked; RESULT [F458] malloc_ret=84696890 r4=00000000 r5=8115D7C7 r2=00000000 sp=A05FFED8 (n=1) - malloc-return site NOW RUNS and malloc returns VALID pointer 0x84696890 (before fix [F458] ZERO); sl=0 crash at 0x8115D28C GONE; new BADMEM moved to guest va=0x00000000 unmapped block=0x8115F9D4 ring 8115F634 812B2260 8115F... another step forward in allocator/setup area; ALSO output contains REAL GAME DEBUG STRING E:/P3DP5D/xrd757/program/app/app_system/system/appAllocatorHandler/appAllocatorHandler.c:%d - proof guest executing real appAllocatorHandler code path; GXM=0 FIOS=0 still (rendering/asset loading not reached yet); NEXT analyze new BADMEM at 0x8115F9D4 (ring 0x8115F634/0x812B2260/0x8115F...) disassemble faulting block check which register/value is 0 = next allocator-setup cursor; CORE AOT CALL-MODEL FIX (LR for indirect calls) VALIDATED"),
    ("18.4031", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6jy: GENERATOR BUG PINPOINTED - INDIRECT CALLS (blx reg) GENERATED WITHOUT SETTING LR: (1) normal bl block correct s->r[14]=0x81015F6Au; return 0x81173194u; /* bl */ (blk_81015F62 batch_001.cpp:10899 LR set to return address); (2) indirect call blx reg generated by generator line 286 as ONLY return id_reg(ridx(ri), s); (blk_8115F448 batch_010.cpp, other examples blk_81000CA6/blk_8100130E) NO s->r[14]=<return address> before it; ROOT CAUSE callee sees stale LR overwrites it with own bl returns to wrong place continuation block blk_8115F458 never runs; FIX in generator when emitting id_reg/blx prepend s->r[14] = <pc of next instruction> (last.address + last.size i.e. address right after blx) exactly like normal bl path; regenerate all blocks + relink; NEXT patch _gen_split.py line ~286 regenerate (py -3 _gen_split.py 500 4) relink run 10M check [F458] fires and sl=0 crash gone = CORE AOT CALL-MODEL FIX"),
    ("18.4030", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6jx: FOUND IT - INDIRECT CALL (return id_reg(6, s)) IS THE PROBLEM: generated blk_8115F448 ends with ... s->r[1]=0x4u; setf_nz; return id_reg(6, s) -> blx r6 implemented as return id_reg(6,s) INDIRECT CALL helper returning target pc; confirmed blk_8115F456 does NOT exist as block (blx is last instruction of 0x8115F448 block) and blk_8115F458 DOES exist (batch_010.cpp:3487) so return address 0x8115F458 has a block; YET [F458] probe never fires -> indirect call returns pc NOT 0x8115F458 -> LR/return address for indirect call not set correctly by call model: id_reg(6,s) returns TARGET pc but does not arrange s->r[14]=0x8115F458 before callee runs; callee (0x8115D7BE malloc wrapper) does bl 0x8115D1F0 which OVERWRITES LR then pop {r4,pc} returns to WRONG address -> function never reaches 0x8115F458 and caller stack/canary state inconsistent producing sl=0 crash at 0x8115D28C; NEXT read id_reg implementation and call-site return-address mechanism; ensure s->r[14]=continuation pc for blx/indirect calls; CORE AOT-CALL-MODEL BUG not game logic"),
    ("18.4029", "static recompilation stage 6jw: DETAIL PROBES - malloc call DOES NOT RETURN to 0x8115F458: [F448] cap raised 8->200 probe fired 72 times IDENTICAL args cb=8115D7BF a1=8115D7C7 a2=0 a3=0x3D size=0x51 sp=A05FFEE8 cur=846867F0; BUT [F458] probe (block right after blx r6 at 0x8115F456 = malloc-return site) produced ZERO output -> execution enters 0x8115F448 reaches blx r6 but NEVER reaches 0x8115F458 (block storing result into new object); later BADMEM still at 0x8115D28C with sl=0; means blx r6 (target 0x8115D7BF malloc wrapper) either (a) not a real call in AOT model (0x8115F456/0x8115F458 merged/split incorrectly so probe pc never equals 0x8115F458) (b) call returns somewhere else (register/LR corruption) (c) block at 0x8115F458 does not exist as entry; NEXT check whether blk_8115F458 exists in generated batches (block boundary after blx) and whether 0x8115F456 is its own block (indirect call site with recorded return 0x8115F458); also instrument target block 0x8115D7BE to see whether it runs and what it returns"),
    ("18.4028", "static recompilation stage 6jv: completed malloc call-chain + found CONTRADICTION: 0x8115D7BE callback -> 0x8115D1F0 -> 0x8115D200 -> 0x811DA534 (push {r4,lr}; bl 0x811E6A08; pop) -> 0x811E6A08 (push {r4,lr}; blx 0x812B22A0; pop) -> 0x812B22A0 = HLE malloc (confirmed by harness header comment 0x812B22A0 malloc); chain DOES reach HLE; hle_malloc cannot plausibly fail for n=0x51: heap_ptr starts 0x82800000 heap_end=0x82E00000 (6MB), [HM] log only 8 allocations sizes 0x4000/0x50000/0x100A0; CONTRADICTION malloc should return valid pointer yet sl ends up 0; suspects (a) blx r6 in 0x8115F448 not actually executed/called with intended r6 (register clobbered), (b) malloc return fine but CALLER path zeroes sl, (c) crash-time [F448] is DIFFERENT call site where r6 is 0 - probe only printed first 8 hits (g_f448_n < 8); NEXT raise [F448] probe cap + print BEFORE/AFTER of blx r6 (block after 0x8115F456 with malloc return value) + log every hle_malloc call return to see whether failing size arrives"),
    ("18.4027", "static recompilation stage 6ju: disassembled callback target 0x8115D7BF: ODD Thumb address real entry 0x8115D7BE = push {r4,lr}; bl 0x8115D1F0; pop {r4,pc} = malloc wrapper (0x8115D1F0 -> 0x8115D200 -> 0x811DA534); also 0x8115D7B0 = size-check helper cmp.w r0,#0x100000; bhi 0x8115D7BA; movs r0,#3; 0x8115D7BA movs r0,#0; bx lr (returns 3 for size <=1MB else 0); r6 callback in 0x8115F448 is indeed malloc called with size 0x51 (normal allocation); YET [HM] logged ONLY 8 EARLY heap allocations (0x4000/0x50000/0x100A0 fiber objects) and NEVER the failing 0x51 allocation -> crash-time malloc does NOT reach HLE hle_malloc: guest malloc chain 0x811DA534 fails/returns 0 internally before delegating to HLE; NEXT disassemble 0x811DA534 (guest malloc) find why returns 0 without calling HLE - likely dereferences uninitialized allocator function pointer (global set up by init routine we never ran / HLE stub returns 0) or checks malloc-enabled flag; fix that init/HLE so allocation proceeds"),
    ("18.4026", "★★ static recompilation stage 6jt: INSTRUMENTED allocator-callback call - HLE HEAP NOT THE CULPRIT: [F448] cb=8115D7BF a1=8115D7C7 a2=00000000 a3=0000003D size=00000051 sp=A05FFEE8 cur=846867F0 (n=1..8) -> callback r6 is 0x8115D7BF a GUEST function NOT malloc wrappers (0x8115D200/0x8115D1F0), called with a1=0x8115D7C7 a2=0 a3=0x3D computed size 0x51; [HM] heap log only 8 allocations ALL SUCCESSFUL: n=00004000 -> 84621390, n=00050000 -> 84625430, n=000100A0 -> 84676750 (fiber1 object), n=000100A0 -> 846867F0 (fiber2 object), heap_ptr=82800000 -> hle_malloc never failed; 0 return comes from GUEST callback 0x8115D7BF own logic (or HLE call inside it); cur=846867F0 fiber2 - failing path now runs in fiber2 (switch fix working); NEXT disassemble 0x8115D7BF and 0x8115D7C7 see what callback does and why returns 0 (calls sceKernel memblock/alloc our HLE stubs return 0, or checks size/condition fails), fix specific HLE or precondition"),
    ("18.4025", "static recompilation stage 6js: identified allocator wrappers before faulting function - 0x8115D200 push {r4,lr}; bl 0x811DA534 (MALLOC wrapper); pop; 0x8115D208 push {r4,lr}; bl 0x811DA554 (FREE wrapper); pop; 0x8115D1F0/0x8115D1F8 thin wrappers around them; callback r6 passed to 0x8115F448 almost certainly one of these malloc wrappers and 0 return means HLE heap allocation FAILED (hle_malloc returned 0); NEXT instrument blx r6 in 0x8115F448 print callback address r6 + requested size r3+0x14 + heap state (free/used bytes), fix allocation (size absurd/parsed wrong/untrusted value or arena exhausted) = allocator-level root of new BADMEM chain"),
    ("18.4024", "static recompilation stage 6jr: identified 0x8115F448 (structure creator whose 0 return causes new crash) = GUEST function, small ALLOCATOR-CALLBACK WRAPPER: push {r4,r5,r6,lr}; adds r5,r1,#0; adds r6,r0,#0; adds r4,r2,#0; adds.w r0,r3,#0x14; movs r1,#4; blx r6; str r4,[r0,#8]; str r6,[r0]; str r5,[r0,#4]; str r2,[r0,#0x10]; pop -> calls blx r6 where r6 = FIRST PARAMETER (r0) = callback/allocator function pointer, computes r0=r3+0x14 as callback size arg, returns whatever callback returns; sl=0 => CALLBACK RETURNED 0 (allocation failed); also 0x812B2260 = SceLibc NID 6DC1F0D8 (memset-like init); NEXT disassemble caller chain before 0x8115D220 (function doing bl 0x8115F448 with r0=callback pointer) find which callback/allocator passed - likely guest malloc wrapper ultimately calling HLE heap; if returns 0 heap/args wrong (size r3+0x14 too large or HLE malloc returned 0 for unaligned/oversize request); then fix allocation path"),
    ("18.4023", "static recompilation stage 6jq: disassembled prologue before new fault - 8115D242 bl 0x8115F448 then 8115D246 mov sl,r0 -> SL is RETURN VALUE of 0x8115F448, followed by 8115D248 add sb,sl,#0x14; 8115D24C mov r0,sb; 8115D250 movs r1,#0; 8115D252 blx 0x812B2260 (memset/init of structure at sl+0x14 using size fp), then stores into [sl+0x14]/[sl+0x18]/[sl+0x1c]/[sl+0x24]/[sl+0x28]/[sl+0x2c] and array loop at [sl+0x20]; fault ldr r0,[sl+0x20] with sl=0 -> ROOT CAUSE 0x8115F448 returned 0 (structure allocation/creation failed); NEXT identify 0x8115F448 (veneer? malloc-like) and 0x812B2260 (init call) in veneer_map/harness, find why creation returns 0 (HLE allocator returns 0 for size/args or prerequisite missing), fix so structure created and array iteration proceeds"),
    ("18.4022", "static recompilation stage 6jp: analyzed NEW BADMEM after fiber-switch fix - [BADMEM] guest va=0x00000020 unmapped block=0x8115D28C ring 812B1B70 812067B6 81206...; faulting block MOVED to 0x8115D2xx region (previously 0x812068xx) - guest now executes further fiber/task code; disasm 0x8115D270 movs r8,#0; str r0,[sl,#0x1c]; str r6,[sl,#0x20]; beq; ldr r0,[sl,#0x1c]; bl 0x81173194; 0x8115D28C ldr r0,[sl,#0x20]; add r8,#1; adds r4,#8; cmp r8,r0; blo 0x8115D282; generated blk_8115D28C s->r[0]=rd32(s->r[10]+0x20) -> ARRAY-ITERATION function (r8 counter, r4 stride 8, per-element call 0x81173194, upper bound [sl+0x20]) whose structure pointer sl (=r10) is ZERO -> va=0x20; ring shows reached from fiber-manager path (GetSelf 812B1B70 -> 812067B6 -> 81206xx); NEXT disassemble function prologue before 0x8115D270 find where sl/r10 set by caller, trace caller passing sl=0, repair argument or initialize structure so iteration proceeds"),
    ("18.4021", "★★ static recompilation stage 6jo: implemented fiber FCtx auto-create on unknown target (switch handler reads fiber object [fiber+0x84] user entry and [fiber+0x88] argOnRun, calls fiber_load, retries g_fctx.find); RESULT [FIBER-AUTOCREATE] fired (t=846867F0 entry=81198C0B arg=82EFFF28) and switch now happens REPEATEDLY ([FEVT] switch cur=84676750 to=846867F0 many times, previously only once) -> switch mechanism FIXED; BUT GXM calls still 0, FIOS opens still 0, run now CRASHES again (BADMEM 2, 10M exit=3) - fiber2 execution after successful switch triggers new fault (progress-by-moving-fault pattern); NEXT capture new BADMEM details (faulting block/va and ring) from err10m_autocreate.txt, disassemble around faulting block, apply same class of repair (resume/entry precondition, missing object)"),
    ("18.4020", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6jn: FIBER SWITCH FAILING WITH unknown target = THE LOOP - 10M grep: [FEVT] switch cur=84676750 to=846867F0 runs=1 (only ONE switch ever), [SWP] fb=846867F0 in=1 cur=84676750 sp=A0DFFFE8 MANY times (sceFiberSwitch(fiber2) called repeatedly inside fiber_exec only arms g_fiber_switch_to), [FIBER-SW] unknown target 846867F0 appears; fiber1 repeatedly calls sceFiberSwitch(fiber2) deferred switch consumed by fiber_exec but g_fctx.find(fiber2) FAILS - fiber2 NOT registered in g_fctx - switch handler logs unknown target breaks and fiber1 keeps retrying forever; ROOT CAUSE fiber2 FCtx never created via fiber_load (only path that populates g_fctx for new fiber) because earlier flow created fiber OBJECT (0x81206700) but never loaded/resumed it; FIX in switch handler when target fiber missing from g_fctx CREATE its FCtx on the spot (fiber_load(s, t, entry from [fiber+0x84], arg from [fiber+0x88]) and proceed instead of breaking; NEXT implement auto-create on unknown target + 10M -> switch should succeed fiber2 task should run game should advance past fiber-manager loop"),
    ("18.4019", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6jm: DECISIVE ACTIVITY ANALYSIS of 10M run: GXM CALLS 0, FIOS OPENS 0, LOOP STARTS VERY EARLY - grep over out10m_flistfix.txt [GXM-BEGIN]/[GXM-PRESENT]/[GXM-CTX] count 0, FIOS OPEN 0, [GFX] periodic stats never appeared; FIRST [PROG] lines already fiber region n=5000 pc=8120685A last_block=812068D8 sp=82EFFE68 r0=0, n=10000 pc=812068A0 last_block=81206894, n=15000 pc=8120685A, n=20000 pc=812068A0 -> from very beginning guest cycling 0x812068xx fiber-manager region and NEVER reaches asset loading (FIOS) or rendering (GXM); CONCLUSION fiber task loop spinning WITHOUT advancing game main workflow (scheduler tasks fiber1/fiber2 per-frame work not producing progress); earlier 3M runs DID open files (57,438 FIOS opens per M428) so something added since changed flow early on (or those opens under previous crash path); NEXT determine what fiber2 task does per cycle - dump distinct pc sequence for fiber2 right after each switch (pcs executed between switch-in and switch-out); if fiber2 task empty/instant its user entry or task body not executed (wrong entry point or task returns immediately because condition/HLE result differs) which would explain zero asset/render progress"),
    ("18.4018", "static recompilation stage 6jl: read g_fiber_switch_to consumption path - fiber_exec_to_completion line 702 main loop 722 consumes deferred switch at line 726 (g_fiber_switch_to -> t; fiber_save; g_fctx.find(t); if target pc==0 restart from user entry; g_cur_fiber=t; memcpy(s->r)); NESTED-REFUSED guard 704-713; deferred switch IS consumed; REVISED busy-wait chain: fiber1 runs completion 0x812067A0 sets [fiber1+0x80]|=2 removal logic switches to head fiber2 HLE arms g_fiber_switch_to fiber_exec consumes switches fiber2 runs task finishes switch handler restarts it (738-748) or returns to fiber1 -> fiber1 completion again = repeated fiber1<->fiber2 completion loop; may be normal per-frame fiber cycle BUT [PROG] pc never leaves 0x812067xx-0x812068xx across 10M blocks -> no progress into next game phase; NEXT instrument what each fiber does per cycle (distinct pcs / FIOS opens / GXM calls per 100k blocks) see if real work happens, check fiber2 completion path - if it completes immediately its user entry (scheduler task) may be wrong"),
    ("18.4017", "static recompilation stage 6jk: tried fiber-list repair (fiber2.next=fiber1 when asymmetric): [FLISTFIX] fired 5+ times (fiber2.next 0 -> fiber1 sp=A0DFFFE8 cur=84676750 n=1..5) but game REWRITES fiber2.next back to 0 every round - repair NOT persistent because COMPLETION FUNCTION itself zeroes links as part of removing fiber; [PROG] at 10M still same fiber state region (pc=8120682A last=812B1BA0 / pc=8120680E last=81206806 / pc=812067C8 last=812067B6 / pc=81206822 last=81206820) loop did NOT exit; BADMEM 0 stable; REVISED understanding: complete/remove fiber1 -> head=fiber2 -> cmp r3,r0 NOT equal -> call sceFiberSwitch -> inside fiber_exec HLE defers via g_fiber_switch_to and returns -> fiber_exec_to_completion switch handler apparently never processes g_fiber_switch_to -> same fiber loops re-removing itself; NEXT inspect how g_fiber_switch_to consumed (fiber_exec_to_completion/dispatch loop) make deferred switch actually happen or make removed fiber stop running"),
    ("18.4016", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6jj: FIBER LIST ASYMMETRIC = ROOT CAUSE OF BUSY-WAIT - [FLIST2] at block 0x8120682A: h18=0 h1c=846867F0 (head=fiber2 non-zero) f1p=846867F0 f1n=0 f2p=0 f2n=0 r3=84676750 cur=84676750 (n=1..10); decoding global list head [0x816CBC08+0xa1c]=0x846867F0 fiber2, fiber1.prev [fiber1+0x94]=0x846867F0 fiber2, fiber1.next=0, fiber2.prev=0, fiber2.next=0, completion function running for r3=fiber1 0x84676750; BUG list ASYMMETRIC - fiber1.prev points to fiber2 but fiber2.next does NOT point back to fiber1 (0); removal logic r2=fiber1.prev=fiber2 writes as new head ([r4,#0xa1c]=0x846867F0) then compares removed fiber r3=fiber1 with new head r0=0x846867F0 NOT equal so calls sceFiberSwitch and loops forever; fiber2.next==0 list never walked to fiber1; FIX repair fiber2.next to fiber1 ([0x846867F0+0x98]=0x84676750) or keep prev/next symmetric; NEXT apply one-value list repair + 10M confirm loop exits and game proceeds"),
    ("18.4015", "static recompilation stage 6ji: identified HLE 0x812B1BA0 = SceFiber NID E4283144 sceFiberSwitch, read harness case line 379: fairly complete impl - cooperative round-robin at main-loop level (every 100th switch runs another fiber via fiber_load + fiber_exec_to_completion), defers switches from inside fiber_exec (g_fiber_switch_to), handles self-switch/yield; at end uint32_t fb = s->r[0] & ~1u; if (!fb) { r0 = 0; break; } if (g_in_fiber_exec) { if (fb != g_cur_fiber) g_fiber_switch_to = fb; r0 = 0; break; } if (fb == g_cur_fiber){...}; KEY: when target fiber is ZERO HLE returns 0 WITHOUT switching; in busy-wait loop game calls 0x812B1BA0 with GLOBAL FIBER-LIST HEAD (loaded from 0x816CBC08+0xa1c at 0x81206818); if that head is 0 HLE does nothing and completion manager loops forever -> likely remaining defect is FIBER LIST STATE: global head at [0x816CBC08+0xa1c] zero when game expects real next-fiber, or fiber prev/next links ([fiber+0x94]/[fiber+0x98]) inconsistent so removal never reaches cmp r3,r0 beq exit; NEXT instrument [0x816CBC08+0xa18], [0x816CBC08+0xa1c], [fiber+0x94]/[fiber+0x98] for fiber1/fiber2 around completion function, fix list state or make HLE handle fb==0 as no-op-with-progress"),
    ("18.4014", "static recompilation stage 6jh: disassembled full loop body 0x812067C8-0x8120682A = FIBER REMOVAL/COMPLETION function 0x812067A0: ldr r1,[r3,#0x98] fiber->next; cbz; str r2,[r1,#0x94] link prev; ldr r2,[r3,#0x94] fiber->prev; str r2,[r4,#0xa1c] global list head=0x816CBC08+0xa1c; cbz; str r1,[r2,#0x98]; ldr r1,[r3,#0x80] state; orrs r1,#2 str r1,[r3,#0x80] SET COMPLETION BIT; cbnz r0; ldr r0,[r0,#0xa1c] global head; cmp r3,r0; beq 0x8120682A; cbz r0,0x8120682A; else movs r1,#0 movs r2,#0 blx 0x812B1BA0 (HLE probably sceFiberSwitch/Run/schedule); 0x8120682A canary check return -> function completes fiber sets bit1 then if removed fiber NOT global head calls 0x812B1BA0; [PROG] loop re-entered repeatedly with fiber2 r0=846867F0 polls completion path every frame/task round loop never advances; MOST LIKELY our HLE 0x812B1BA0 does not do what real sceFiber function does (e.g. should SWITCH to another fiber and not return) so control falls through and manager re-runs same completion forever; NEXT identify HLE 0x812B1BA0 in veneer_map + harness impl, check fiber list state (prev/next/head) around function - loop should exit once completed fiber IS head or switch actually happens"),
    ("18.4013", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6jg: LOGGING OPTIMIZATION + NEW FINDING - [AFTER] was 492,961 of first 500,000 lines (98.6%) = cause of 1.3GB output; capped with g_after_total++ < 400 -> 10M exit=0 elapsed=2.2s (was 1035s), out size 1.3MB (was 1.3GB), BADMEM 0; harness now fast for rapid iteration (50M ~11s); NEW FINDING [PROG] lines at n=9.975M-10M: guest STILL cycling fiber state region pc=81206820 last=8120681C / pc=812067E8 last=812067DC / pc=8120682A last=812B1BA0 / pc=8120680E last=81206806 / pc=812067C8 last=812067B6 / pc=81206822 last=81206820 all sp=A0DFFFE8 r0=846867F0 (fiber2) -> BUSY-WAIT LOOP in fiber state machine polling something that never becomes true (very likely fiber2 completion bit [fiber+0x80]&2 or related status HLE never sets); NEXT analyze loop 0x812067C8-0x8120682A waiting condition, set expected status (e.g. fiber2 completion bit) so loop exits and game proceeds"),
    ("18.4012", "★★★★ static recompilation stage 6jf: 10M-BLOCK RUN COMPLETES CLEAN (exit=0, ZERO BADMEM) - 10M run exit=0 elapsed=1035s, BADMEM count 0, guest runs 10M blocks without a single memory fault; output size 1.3GB (verbose per-block probes still enabled); KEY PROGRESS LINES: [PATH] job_resource_%d / job_update_%d / job_render_%d (game loading job/render resource path templates), [GXMVK] present frame=1/2/3 image=0/1/2 result=0, [INJECT] load-request chain head=846ACC40 count=300 (CPK injection at block 20000), [PMP2] pass #1 blocks=50, after blk 118/119/120; game no longer crashes and is progressing through init/resource-loading phase; NEXT (a) reduce verbose logging so runs fast + outputs small (b) run 50M classify phases (c) look for first real rendering path (GXM BeginScene calls) and FIOS asset opens"),
    ("18.4011", "★★★★ static recompilation stage 6je: BADMEM IS GONE - 3M RUN COMPLETES exit=0! Hoisted r5 repair above g_682a_n<20 counter gate both dispatch copies: if ((pc & ~1u) == 0x8120682A && r5 == 0) r5 = 0x812B414C (every visit repaired, not just first 20). RESULT 3M run exit=0 previously ALWAYS exit=3 with BADMEM, NO [BADMEM] output at all, PMP2 passes=1, run completes normally at block limit - FIRST CLEAN 3M RUN since crash chain began (0x94 -> 0x00 -> 0x80 -> ... -> gone). Long crash hunt from BADMEM va=0x94 block 0x812067B6 now FULLY RESOLVED through chain: stale-fn M448, resume-point emulation M452, canary-slot M463/M464, relaxed r5 repair M469, hoist outside counter gate M471. NEXT run LONGER (10M/50M blocks) see whether game progresses into new phases (scene loader, GXM/render calls, FIOS asset loads) and whether new crashes appear; capture new output"),
    ("18.4010", "static recompilation stage 6jd: analyzed NEW ring from relaxed-r5 run - full BADMEM guest va=0x00000000 unmapped block=0x8120682A ring 812067EA 81206806 8120680E 8120681C...; blocks are fiber state-management (0x812067EA str r1,[r2,#0x98] ldr r1,[r3,#0x80]; 0x81206806 orrs r1,#2 str r1,[r3,#0x80]; 0x8120680E cbnz r0,0x8120681C; 0x8120681C cmp r3,r0 beq 0x8120682A) -> control flows into 0x8120682A, fault STILL ldr r0,[r5]; KEY REALIZATION [682A-R5FIX] sits INSIDE probe gated by g_682a_n++ < 20 so only first 20 visits repaired, later visits (real crash after 19-20 prints) get r5=0 unrepaired -> va=0; FIX move r5 repair OUTSIDE g_682a_n<20 gate or raise limit so r5=0 repaired on EVERY visit to block 0x8120682A; NEXT hoist r5 fix above counter check both dispatch copies + 3M"),
    ("18.4009", "static recompilation stage 6jc: relaxed r5 repair - inside 0x8120682A probe if r5==0 set r5=0x812B414C regardless of sp; RESULT [682A-R5FIX] fires 19 times (r5 0 -> 0x812B414C sp=A0DFFFE8) so r5=0 condition real and now repaired; crash still reports BADMEM guest va=0x00000000 unmapped block=0x8120682A BUT ring CHANGED to 812067EA 81206806 8120680E 8120681C... (previously 81206820 81206822 812B1...) -> fault location moved EARLIER in same function region, previous ldr r0,[r5] (r5=0) fault likely fixed and different NULL dereference now on earlier path (e.g. ldr.w r0,[r0,#0xa1c] after ldr r0,[0x816CBC08] in 0x8120680E-0x81206818, or cmp/branch into 0x8120681C); NEXT dump full BADMEM ring + exact faulting instruction disassembling blocks 0x812067EA..0x8120681C find NULL register, apply same class of repair; game progressing (fault moved)"),
    ("18.4008", "static recompilation stage 6jb: armed write-watch canary slot 0xA0DFFFD4 after 682A-FIX2 repair, checked every dispatch both loops -> ZERO CWATCH lines: repaired canary slot NOT re-clobbered, canary value stays correct; YET crash persists BADMEM guest va=0x00000000 unmapped block=0x8120682A; block 0x8120682A generated s->r[1]=rd32(s->r[13]+4) s->r[0]=rd32(s->r[5]+0); fault is ldr r0,[r5] with r5=0 (va=0) BEFORE/independent of canary compare; REAL remaining issue r5=0 when block 0x8120682A runs and 682A-FIX2 guard (r5==0 && sp==0xA0DFFFE8) does NOT cover r5==0 but sp different case; FIX widen r5 repair if r5==0 at 0x8120682A set r5=0x812B414C regardless of sp, only adjust stack/canary for 0xA0DFFFE8 signature; NEXT relax condition + 3M"),
    ("18.4007", "static recompilation stage 6ja: read lines 908-940 + FULL line 922 - structure line 918 if ((pc & ~1u) == 0x8120682Au && g_682a_n++ < 20) { -> 919 [682A] -> 920 [CANARY682A] -> 921 [682A-ZERO] -> 922 if (s->r[5]==0u && s->r[13]==0xA0DFFFE8u) { r5=0x812B414C; sp=0xA0DFFFD0; ... _v=0x812B4150u memcpy; printf [682A-FIX2]; } -> fflush; condition SHOULD be satisfied at n=2..5 (r5=0 sp=0xA0DFFFE8 per [682A]), counter 2..5 < 20, printf present -> most likely EARLIER OUTPUT QUERY TRUNCATED (only first 10 matching lines); NEXT grep FULL out3m_canaryfix2.txt for [682A-FIX2] and count; if present emulation runs but canary slot re-clobbered between fix and next [682A] check (saved back to 0x81198BEE) -> watch exact address [sp+4]=0xA0DFFFD4 for writes find re-clobbering block"),
