    ("18.3991", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6iu: FOUND BAD FCtx - [682A-ZERO] fctx: 84676750:pc=812067B6 sp=A0DFFFE8 r5=00000000 846867F0:pc=00000000 sp=A05FFF08 r5=00000001 -> fiber1 stored FCtx INCONSISTENT: pc=suspend point 0x812067B6 but sp=0xA0DFFFE8 (0x812067A0 ENTRY sp) and r5=0 (ENTRY value) = some save path stored entry-state context with suspend pc; correct FSAVE pc=812067B6 sp=A0DFFFD0 r5=812B414C so a LATER save overwrote proper context; resuming from bad FCtx starts 0x8120682A r5=0 -> BADMEM va=0; FIX pragmatic at 0x8120682A if r5==0 emulate 0x812067A0 prologue (r5=0x812B414C sp=0xA0DFFFD0); ROOT-CAUSE later find save storing entry-state context; NEXT apply prologue emulation (guard r5==0 && sp==0xA0DFFFE8) + 3M"),
    ("18.3990", "★★ static recompilation stage 6it: resume-point instrumentation decisive - [682A] fires TWICE: (n=1) r5=812B414C r13=A0DFFFD0 r14=8120682A cur=84676750 NORMAL; (n=2) r5=00000000 r13=A0DFFFE8 r0=0 r1=0 r14=8120682A cur=84676750 CRASH (r5=0 AND sp=0xA0DFFFE8 = 0x812067A0 ENTRY sp, as if entering fresh without prologue); all fiber1 FSAVE pc=812067B6 sp=A0DFFFD0 r5=812B414C x3 -> second 0x8120682A does NOT come from correctly-saved fiber1 context, comes from DIFFERENT FCtx with sp=0xA0DFFFE8 and r5=0 (some save/restore path likely switch path line ~733 memcpy(s->r, it->second.r) or rebuilt FCtx); FIX DIRECTION resume into 0x8120682A must use fiber1 FSAVE context (sp=0xA0DFFFD0 r5=0x812B414C) or re-run 0x812067A0 prologue; NEXT find which FCtx has sp=0xA0DFFFE8/r5=0 (print all fibers FSAVE + switch restore at 0x8120682A) fix that restore"),
