    ("18.3984", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6in: DOUBLE-CONTROL-FLOW TIMELINE decisive - L650 FLOAD fiber1 f84=81198BE9 arg=846867F0; L651 FL2 fiber1 entry=81206BDC sp=A0E00000; L665 [5928] cur=84676750 sp=A0DFFFE8 r14=81198BEE n=1 (normal init); L701 FEVT switch cur=84676750 to=846867F0; L702/L704/L705 FSAVE fiber1 pc=812067B6 sp=A0DFFFD0 x3 (SUSPENDED); L703 FIBER-SW unknown target 846867F0; L6496 FLOAD fiber2 f84=81198C0B f88=82EFFF28; L6498 FLOAD-BAD fiber2 r13=A0600000; L6710 [5928] cur=84676750 sp=A0DFFFE0 r14=81198BEE n=2 -> after suspension fiber1 RESTARTED FROM LOADER CHAIN (sp=0xA0DFFFE0 not suspended 0xA0DFFFD0) = SECOND control flow on same stack; second flow prologue overwrites suspended frame 0xA0DFFFD0 -> resumed fiber1 reads 0 -> BADMEM 0x94; bug is fiber1 RE-ENTRY after suspension (not prologue); next find trigger after L702 (FEVT/switch + loader loop L6498-L6710) then mark fiber1 BUSY on suspension or route restart to fresh context/stack"),
    ("18.3983", "★★ static recompilation stage 6im: [5928] instrumentation (string replacement) shows 0x811E5928 executes TWICE both on FIBER1: [5928] cur=84676750 sp=A0DFFFE8 r14=81198BEE r0=811E5929 (n=1) and cur=84676750 sp=A0DFFFE0 r14=81198BEE r0=811E5929 (n=2); r14=0x81198BEE is fiber1 loader return (normal init chain); FSAVE fiber1 saved pc=0x812067B6 sp=0xA0DFFFD0 3x -> SAME fiber1 has TWO live stack frames: (a) suspended pc=0x812067B6 sp=0xA0DFFFD0 (b) executing loader chain sp=0xA0DFFFE8/0xA0DFFFE0; 0x811E5928 entered sp=0xA0DFFFE0 push covers [0xA0DFFFBC..A0DFFFE0) overwrites suspended slot 0xA0DFFFD0 -> resumed fiber1 reads reused/zeroed frame -> BADMEM 0x94; SCHEDULER-CORRECTNESS bug (pump runs fiber1 loader chain while fiber1 suspended, or resumes without restoring stack); next inspect pump/switch decision, whether fiber1 should be busy during suspension and whether save should copy stack or reject/queue suspension"),
    ("18.3982", "static recompilation stage 6il: fiber1 switched out at crash pc THREE TIMES - [FSAVE] fiber=84676750 pc=812067B6 sp=A0DFFFD0 appears 3x (after [FL2] fiber=84676750 entry=81206BDC sp=A0E00000 r0=84676750) -> fiber1 repeatedly saved at pc=0x812067B6 sp=0xA0DFFFD0 (exact pc/sp pair that later reads clobbered slot); [5928] instrumentation failed to build due to Python %-format bug in patch script (chk percent with s-arrow arg treats C %08X as Python format -> TypeError); next rebuild [5928] with string replacement, re-run to see which fiber executes 0x811E5928 + its sp + FSAVE/FL2 sequence around the 3 switches at pc=0x812067B6, whether resumed between saves and whether resume restores sp=0xA0DFFFD0 stale frame"),
    ("18.3981", "★ static recompilation stage 6ik: window dump clarifies mechanism - [WSLOT-WIN] A0DFFFC0..DC = 00000000 x7 then 81198BEE (fiber1 loader return), pre-tail 811E5CDA 811E5CE8 811E5928 81207344 -> ENTIRE 0xA0DFFFC0..0xA0DFFFD8 zeroed in one go (only 0xA0DFFFDC valid), consistent with 0x811E5928 prologue push 9 + sub 0x424; CORRECTED MATH: 0x811E5928 entered sp=0xA0DFFFE0 -> push 9 -> sp=0xA0DFFFBC writing [0xA0DFFFBC..A0DFFFE0) INCLUDING 0xA0DFFFD0, sub 0x424 -> sp=0xA0DFFB98 (matches observed) -> zero at 0xA0DFFFD0 is a saved zero register, slot REUSED as callee frame (normal); REAL BUG: fiber1 SUSPENDED at 0x812067B6 sp=0xA0DFFFD0 (FSAVE) but same fiber1 stack later used by 0x811E5928 call overwriting suspended frame -> scheduler resumes with stale frame or fiber1 never really suspended; next trace fiber1 lifecycle around FSAVE pc=0x812067B6 (who runs 0x811E5928 after suspension on which fiber; does fiber_load restore pc=0x812067B6 sp=0xA0DFFFD0 stale frame) -> reconcile save/restore with call chain"),
    ("18.3980", "static recompilation stage 6ij: added [WSLOT-HLE] at end of hle_call (before return s->r[14], print g_cur_block) - NO output -> when sceFiberGetSelf returns slot 0xA0DFFFD0 still 0x84676750 (unchanged), so zero-write NOT inside HLE/return; combined with [WSLOT-RG] prev=0x811E5928 now=0x81207344 old=84676750 new=0 -> zero during next dispatched block(s); BUT address math says 0x811E5928 prologue (push 9 from sp=0xA0DFFFD0 writes [A0DFFFAC..A0DFFFD0), sub 0x424, canary [sp+0x420]=0xA0DFFFB8) does NOT write 0xA0DFFFD0 -> contradiction; next dump full context inside [WSLOT-RG] hit (g_cur_block pc sp g_ws_snap slot value prev 4 g_pre_pc) + check after each of first 2-3 blocks of 0x811E5928 + verify g_ws_snap not overwritten"),
    ("18.3979", "static recompilation stage 6ii: disassembled 0x811E5900-0x811E5940 + blk_811E5928 - it is a LARGE-STACK-FRAME prologue (push.w 9 regs=36B, subw sp,#0x424, store [0x812B414C] at [sp,#0x420] canary, then bl 0x81207344), matches M159 stack-leak note; ADDRESS MATH: 0x812067A0 push{r4,r5,lr}+sub sp,#0xc -> sp=0xA0DFFFD0 [sp]==GetSelf out; 0x811E5928 entered sp=0xA0DFFFD0, push 9 writes [0xA0DFFFAC..A0DFFFD0) (last write 0xA0DFFFAC), sub 0x424 -> sp=0xA0DFFB98 (matches WSLOT); prologue push does NOT include 0xA0DFFFD0 and blk_811E5928 has no HLE call -> WSLOT attribution prev=0x811E5928 likely just last-block-before-check; real zero-write in GetSelf-return -> next-block transition (HLE return path or next dispatched block); next check slot immediately AFTER GetSelf case returns inside hle_call + print canary [sp+0x420] vs [0x812B414C]"),
    ("18.3978", "★★ static recompilation stage 6ih THE SLOT CLOBBERER IS CAUGHT: write-watch armed in sceFiberGetSelf when out==0xA0DFFFD0 (snap=0x84676750 the fiber value just written), checked before every block in BOTH loops -> [WS-ARM] snap=84676750 then [WSLOT-RG] prev=811E5928 now=81207344 sp=A0DFFB98 old=84676750 new=00000000 cur=84676750 -> after block 0x811E5928 executes the saved slot 0xA0DFFFD0 flips 0x84676750 -> 0 (direct cause of BADMEM 0x94, fiber1 resume reads 0 -> ldr [r3+0x94]); next read generated code of blk_811E5928 + caller chain 0x81207344 - likely memset/memcpy-class HLE wrapper with wrong destination (writes 0 to 0xA0DFFFxx stack) or block storing 0 to wrong pointer; fix to unblock fiber1/init"),
    ("18.3977", "static recompilation stage 6ig: audited fiber_save (line 633: only memcpy(c.r,s->r)+apsr, no stack copy/zero) / fiber_load (line 639: does NOT reset SP, memcpy(s->r,c.r)) / FIBER-SW (line 718-741: fiber_save; g_fctx.find(t); if pc==0 rebuild from entry sp=0xA0E00000-idx*0x800000; `if (it == g_fctx.end()) { printf FIBER-SW unknown target; break; }` -> for unknown 0x846867F0 the switch is ABANDONED and fiber_exec breaks); CONCLUSION save/load path does not zero the slot -> [0xA0DFFFD0]=0 written by something running while fiber1 suspended (fiber2 pump/fallout writing into 0xA0DFFF00 region, or hle_malloc overlapping); next write-watch exact address 0xA0DFFFD0 in BOTH loops from GetSelf return until fiber1 resume, print writer pc; also check hle_malloc arena bounds vs 0xA0DFFFxx"),
    ("18.3976", "★ BADMEM 0x94 TRIGGER CONTEXT captured - FIBER-SWITCH side effect not GetSelf failure: [GSDBG] in_exec=1 out=A0DFFFD0 f=84676750 cur=84676750 (GetSelf SUCCEEDS writes f into [0xA0DFFFD0]) then [FEVT] switch cur=84676750 to=846867F0 runs=1, [FSAVE] fiber=84676750 pc=812067B6 sp=A0DFFFD0, [FIBER-SW] unknown target 846867F0 (x2 more FSAVE); when fiber1 resumes at pc=0x812067B6 the value at [0xA0DFFFD0] is ZERO instead of f=0x84676750 -> own fiber switch/save/load path clobbers or never restores saved stack slot; next read fiber_save/fiber_load: (a) FCtx save whole stack or just registers (b) unknown-target branch reset sp/zero memory (c) resume copies saved sp correctly"),
    ("18.3975", "static recompilation stage 6ie: exact GetSelf call site of BADMEM 0x94 found: [HLE] #323 va=812B1B70 lr=812067B6 a0=A0DFFFD0 a1=812B4150 a2=0 - happens ONCE, out a0=0xA0DFFFD0 valid fiber1-stack address (0x812067B0 add r0,sp,#0 so out==sp); other sites lr=0x81206860 x10, 0x8120686C x9; out valid so HLE should write non-zero f and ldr r3,[sp] should be non-zero yet BADMEM reports r3=0 (va=0x94) -> CONTRADICTION candidates: (a) in_fiber_exec=1 but cur/last/list all 0 so f=0x82F00000 fallback, (b) write to out went elsewhere GP(0xA0DFFFD0) failed, (c) GSDBG shows different f; next read [GSDBG] right before [HLE] #323 + verify GP(0xA0DFFFD0) in range"),
    ("18.3974", "static recompilation stage 6id: BADMEM 0x94 MECHANISM IDENTIFIED - disasm 0x812067A0-0x812067C8: blx 0x812B1B70 (sceFiberGetSelf, SceFiber NID 414D8CA5) then ldr r3,[sp]; ldr.w r2,[r3,#0x94] -> block 0x812067B6 dereferences [outValue+0x94]; out=0 gives exactly va=0x94; harness has dummy (thread-level hle_malloc(0xA0), [obj+0x80]|=1, fiber-level g_cur_fiber) and writes f to *out; remaining question why out=0: (a) hle_malloc returned 0, (b) out pointer s->r[0]==0, (c) f==0; next grep [GSDBG]/[GETSELF-DUMMY] (in_exec,out,f,cur) then fix (always write non-zero dummy, static fallback if out==0)"),
    ("18.3973", "static recompilation stage 6ic render pipeline step 5: GXM FRAME PATH WIRED TO VULKAN BACKEND - gxm_vulkan.h adds gxmvk_begin_frame/gxmvk_end_frame/gxmvk_present_now (end_frame placeholder clear+present, first 10 frames logged); recomp_harness.cpp wires GXM HLE cases 0x812B1470 BeginScene->begin_frame, 0x812B17F0 EndScene->end_frame, 0x812B1720 DisplayQueueAddEntry->present_now; relink OK; 3M: Vulkan ready + 3 demo presents OK but NO GXM-BEGIN/ENDSCENE/PRESENT lines -> game still not reached rendering; state unchanged (PMP2=1, after blk 120 pc=0x8120736A, BADMEM 0x94); render pipeline READY end-to-end from HLE side but guest blocked earlier by BADMEM 0x94 -> next priority resolve BADMEM 0x94 (real gate), or start offline GXP->SPIR-V translation"),
    ("18.3972", "★★ RENDER PIPELINE STEP 4: VULKAN BACKEND INTEGRATED INTO THE AOT HARNESS. Created C:/dev/tmp/recomp_split/gxm_vulkan.h (self-contained minimal Vulkan backend: Win32 window+instance+surface+device+swapchain+command pool+per-frame gxmvk_present_clear(r,g,b)); integration: #include in recomp_harness.cpp, gxmvk_init() after load_elf, 3-frame demo clear+present from run_guest loop (after 2000 blocks then every 2000); relink adds -L C:/dev/vulkan -lvulkan-1 -lgdi32 -luser32 (exit 0); 3M RUN: backend ready 624x441 3 swapchain images queue=0, present frame=1/2/3 image=0/1/2 result=0; game continues (PMP2=1, after blk 120 pc=0x8120736A, BADMEM 0x94 unrelated); next: map GXM frame path (sceGxmBeginScene 0x812B1470 / EndScene 0x812B17F0 / DisplayQueueAddEntry 0x812B1720) onto gxmvk, then GXP shader->SPIR-V, textures, render targets, vertex upload"),
    ("18.3971", "★★★ RENDER PIPELINE STEP 3 COMPLETE - FIRST FRAME PRESENTED: C:/dev/tmp/vk_min3.cpp (hand-written Vulkan ABI + vkGetDeviceProcAddr) built and RAN: window OK, surface->0, queue family=0, device->0, caps->0 extent=624x441 minImageCount=2, formats=5 fmt=44, swapchain->0, images=3, submit->0, PRESENT->0 (image 0), stage3 OK exit 0; COMPLETE chain validated: Win32 window -> VkSurfaceKHR -> physical device -> queue family (GRAPHICS+present) -> logical device (VK_KHR_swapchain) -> swapchain 624x441 3 images B8G8R8A8 -> command buffer -> barrier TRANSFER_DST -> clear blue -> barrier PRESENT_SRC -> submit -> vkQueuePresentKHR=VK_SUCCESS; remaining (a) GXM->backend mapping (b) GXP->SPIR-V (c) textures/render targets/samplers (d) vertex/index upload; next stage 4: GXM->Vulkan mapping layer starting with frame path"),
    ("18.3970", "★ RENDER PIPELINE STEP 2: VULKAN STAGE 2 VERIFIED - C:/dev/tmp/vk_min2.cpp (hand-written Vulkan ABI + instance func ptrs via vkGetInstanceProcAddr) built and RAN: window OK, vkCreateInstance->0, vkCreateWin32SurfaceKHR->0, queue families=6 chosen=0, vkCreateDevice->0 (VK_KHR_swapchain), smoke stage2 OK exit 0; present-capable path complete to logical device: Win32 window -> instance (VK_KHR_surface+win32_surface) -> VkSurfaceKHR -> physical device -> queue family (GRAPHICS+present) -> logical device (VK_KHR_swapchain); next stage 3: swapchain (VkSwapchainCreateInfoKHR + caps/formats/present modes) -> render pass + image views -> clear via cmd buffer -> present one frame"),
